window.AKK_MARQUIS_INNER_VOICE_CHAPTERS=(window.AKK_MARQUIS_INNER_VOICE_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":1,"title":"Chapter 1: System, Let's Unbind Ourselves","paragraphs":["Jiang Yunxi had died.","Then she came back to life.","But how long she could stay alive—hours, days—was still unknown.","“Pain... it hurts so much!!!”","The moment Jiang Yunxi regained even a sliver of consciousness, she was engulfed by endless agony.","They said pain came in thirteen levels. Jiang Yunxi felt that what she was experiencing had to be level fourteen.","The emperor of all emperors.","It was like a massive truck was running over her body again and again.","A fragment of her memories from before she lost consciousness resurfaced.","“So death is this painful.”","She had thought it was a final burst of awareness before death and had quietly waited for her consciousness to fade away. Yet instead, her mind grew clearer and clearer.","“What’s going on? Wasn’t I already dead? Then how...”","“Has Miss woken up yet?”","“Not yet.”","Two unfamiliar voices reached her ears, and Jiang Yunxi froze.","What was this “Miss” business?","Didn’t they call people in hell things like this ghost or that ghost?","Did ghosts need to sleep too?","The next instant, those questions seemed to trigger some kind of switch. Her head throbbed, and a flood of memories came rushing in.","Just as she was about to sort through them, an excited voice rang out in her mind.","【Host, you’re finally awake!】","【Host, I’m your System Sprite.】","Caught completely off guard by the voice, Jiang Yunxi nearly had a heart attack.","She could practically see her great-grandmother waving at her.","【Host, aren’t you surprised? Delighted?】","【I checked your memories. I know you’ve always wanted a storage space and a system!】","A System Sprite... and it was hers!","She had bonded with a system. Did that mean she wasn’t dead after all?","After reading novels for so many years, Jiang Yunxi had seen people bond with systems before—but never ghosts.","What was more, although she had not yet had time to organize the memories that had just flooded into her mind, she had caught glimpses of them.","Those memories did not belong to her.","Memories that weren’t hers, plus a system... as a veteran web-novel reader, Jiang Yunxi arrived at one conclusion.","She had transmigrated.","【System, what exactly is going on?】","【How did you bind to me?】","【Am I still alive?】","System: 【Host, you died, but then you came back to life.】","Jiang Yunxi: The art of saying nothing had truly been mastered by this thing.","Her body hurt too badly for her to waste time bantering with the system, so she impatiently urged, 【Speak plainly.】","System: 【I am speaking plainly.】","Sensing the intense fluctuations in its host’s emotions, the system did not dare keep joking and hurriedly explained.","【When you thought that, since you already had terminal cancer and only had a few days left to live anyway, you might as well trade your life for someone else’s and chose to take a bullet for a Chinese soldier, you died.】","【Completely and utterly dead.】","Jiang Yunxi: 【Then how did I come back to life?】","【Did you save me?】","The System Sprite spoke rapidly.","【To be precise, it was the Chinese soldiers who saved you.】","【It was my first time carrying out a mission. Because I was inexperienced, I went to the wrong time and space and happened to pass over your world.】","The System Sprite’s tone was full of chagrin.","【Those soldiers were desperate to save you after you were critically injured protecting their comrade. Their urgency was so strong, and their magnetic field so intense, that it affected me.","Somehow, I ended up binding with you after your body died and your soul left it.】","【The Main System discovered that I had gone to the wrong time and space—and even bound myself to the wrong host—so it came to correct the mistake.】","Yet, bound by the merit of those soldiers, the military souls and accumulated merit of the entire Huaxia armed forces were protecting you. It couldn’t forcibly sever the bond.","If it accidentally caused your soul to scatter and vanish, the System Realm would have thoroughly offended Huaxia.】","You Huaxia people are not easy to provoke. Setting aside the ancient great powers, even the hosts bound to various systems over the years would form a considerable force if they joined together.","【The Main System had no choice but to make the best of a mistake and kick both your soul and me, your system, into this time and space.】","【The Main System said that hosts can be replaced, but the time and space cannot.】","The Main System had even secretly instructed it to keep a close eye on her and make sure she didn’t get herself killed.","With all that merit and the protection of Huaxia’s military souls, if anything happened to her...","Forget this little shrimp of a system—even the Main System wouldn’t get away unscathed.","Naturally, the system didn’t dare let its host know that. It was afraid she would become reckless, knowing she had nothing to fear.","And then...","Jiang Yunxi understood.","She was glad that, in that moment, she had followed her instincts.","She had traded what little life she had left for the soldiers’ safety, never expecting such an outcome.","She had been given another chance at life, and she even had a system by her side.","She believed that, back in the modern era, the country would not treat her family unfairly.","The money they had borrowed for her treatment should be enough to pay off, and there might even be some left for her parents.","Although she had an older sister, so her parents would not be left without anyone to care for them in their old age, this at least proved that she had not been entirely useless.","This deal, Jiang Yunxi felt, was an absolute steal.","From what the system had just said, she had also picked up some information: apparently, she had powerful backing.","Even the Main System did not dare offend it, much less this little system.","Perhaps, from now on, when she did things...","Fortunately, the system could not access every thought in her mind. Otherwise...","【Why does everything hurt so much?】","【You brought me into this body—did you harm its original owner?】","【If you did harm her, who would be responsible for that?】","With merit protecting her body and all this transmigration business, Jiang Yunxi was beginning to believe in such mystical matters.","If she had harmed the original owner of this body because of her arrival, would that karma fall on the system—or on her?","Surely it could not be her fault. She had not asked the system to place her in this body.","If anyone was to blame, it should be the system—or the Main System!","【Rest assured, Host. Before you entered this body, its original owner had already died.】","【This system is a law-abiding, upstanding system. I would never do something as cruel as taking a life without regard.】","Jiang Yunxi did not feel even the slightest bit embarrassed.","Such matters had to be made clear from the start, otherwise there would be disputes later on.","【Then how did the original owner die?】","【It wasn’t revenge, was it? Am I safe now?】","【My whole body hurts. Is it because the original owner was injured, or because my soul and this body are incompatible and rejecting each other?】","【Can my soul remain in this body?】","【And what kind of system are you?】","【Please don’t tell me you’re some kind of mission system or romance-conquest system.","Let me tell you, I hate doing missions most of all, and I hate having to pursue and win over someone even more.","I’ve been single since birth. I’ve never dated, I don’t know how to date, and I definitely don’t know how to win someone over.】","【If failing missions or being unable to conquer the target means I’ll be erased, then you might as well let me die right now.】","[So I won’t have to spend every day on edge afterward, worrying that one day I might fail to complete a mission...】","Relying on what she believed was her backing, Jiang Yunxi made her stance clear right away: she didn’t want to do missions, and she didn’t want to pursue or win over anyone.","Jiang Yunxi fired off so many questions in a row that she completely stunned the system.","Hadn’t she wanted a system very badly? Why was she being so picky the moment they bonded?","Hosts these days were far too difficult to manage. She was the worst host it had ever had.","The system was deeply relieved that, before the Main System had kicked it over here, it had worried that the host might fail her missions and die, thereby offending Huaxia. So it had modified the system core.","Otherwise...","The system’s silence made Jiang Yunxi’s heart skip a beat. Could the system she’d bonded with really be a mission system—or some kind of romance-conquest system?","Then she was doomed.","She might as well give up immediately.","Having read plenty of novels, she knew those two kinds of systems were complete traps. If you failed a mission or didn’t reach the required affection level, they’d shock you with electricity or strike you with lightning.","Someone like her would be finished sooner or later.","If she was going to die sooner or later anyway, she might as well die sooner and reincarnate sooner.","Maybe, with all that accumulated merit, she could be reborn in Huaxia. Eighteen years later, she’d be a fine young woman again.","【System, let’s unbind.】"]},{"number":2,"title":"Chapter 2: System, I Have It So Hard","paragraphs":["【System, let’s sever our bond!】","The words struck like a thunderbolt out of nowhere, crashing the System’s CPU.","The System never imagined that merely failing to respond in time would earn it a threat from its Host to sever their connection.","It hadn’t even done anything! It had only been thinking about how to answer its Host.","After all, it had originally been designed as a mission system. But then the Main System made a change, giving it the functions of two different systems.","The Main System had instructed it to let its Host enjoy gossip without risk or worry, while also finding a way to have the Host complete the original system missions without her knowing.","If a mission wasn’t completed, the punishment originally meant for the Host would instead fall on it.","Although the severity of the punishment had been reduced somewhat, it would be delayed until after this Host severed their bond, when it would be reflected in the System’s overall KPI evaluation.","When the person who was originally supposed to be punished was the Host, but the punishment had instead become its responsibility, even the System Sprite felt that it was getting a raw deal.","It felt there was nowhere it could go to seek justice.","But the Main System had said that if it hadn’t run into the wrong time-space and accidentally become bound to its current Host while gossiping, none of these troublesome matters would have happened afterward.","If it didn’t take the blame, then who would?","Even so... despite that... it still felt wronged.","It had taken such a huge risk for its Host, and not only did the Host know nothing about it, she was even threatening to sever their bond.","As a novice system binding itself to a Host for the first time, if its Host voluntarily severed the connection right after the binding, the only thing awaiting it would be being sent back for reconstruction.","Its system life was supposed to have begun with it making a name for itself in the world of systems. Instead, it was about to end before it had even started.","It kept its Host in its heart, while its Host kicked it straight into a ditch.","The System was suffering.","The System was crying pitifully.","It hurriedly sought help from the Main System, asking whether it could conceal its identity as a mission system, lest...","It was having such a hard time.","Had the Main System forgotten that it was only a novice system too? Could it really shoulder such a huge responsibility?","You’re afraid of Huaxia and don’t dare let my Host die, so you come bully me instead.","Fortunately, because of Jiang Yunxi’s special nature, the Main System had been paying close attention to the situation on their side. Its reply arrived in an instant.","After receiving the Main System’s response, the System hurriedly answered,","【Host, rest assured. This System is neither a mission system nor a strategy system. It’s merely an ordinary Gossip System.】","Jiang Yunxi felt inexplicably disdainful of the Gossip System. What use was there in binding herself to a gossip system?","Gossip was only good for passing the time!","With that time, she might as well play on her phone or read novels.","Come to think of it, where had she been transported? Were there phones and tablets here?","Jiang Yunxi had received far too many memories, and her entire body was in unbearable pain. She had no mind to sort through them just then, so she simply asked directly,","【System, you still haven’t told me what era this is, or what happened to the original owner of this body.】","【Ding—】","【The Gossip System is now officially at your service.","As for the gossip concerning this body—in other words, you, Host—would you like to hear it?】","Jiang ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌‌​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​‌​​​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​‌‌‌‍Yunxi: 【Tell me.】","How could she refuse? At the very least, this would help her figure out her current identity—and let her see whether this Gossip System was actually any good.","The System inhaled sharply: I’m very good.","The System: 【The original owner of this body was also named Jiang Yunxi.】","Jiang Yunxi: “Good. At least I won’t have to get used to another name.”","[She is currently nine years old, the Fifth Miss of the Marquis of Pingyang’s household, a daughter born to Madam Zheng, the Heir to the Marquis of Pingyang’s Secondary Wife.","Because she was born after a difficult labor that left her in poor health, she had always been kept deep within the inner chambers and rarely went out.]","Jiang Yunxi: “······”","From “the Marquis of Pingyang’s household,” “daughter of a secondary wife,” and “the Heir’s Secondary Wife,” she deduced that she had transmigrated to ancient times.","Wasn’t the modern era perfectly fine? If not that, she could at least have gone to some interstellar future. Why did it have to be ancient times?","Please, let it not be the dynasty with the queue hairstyle.","Jiang Yunxi immediately interrupted the System. [System, don’t tell me I’ve transmigrated into the Qing dynasty, okay?]","[Rest assured, Host. This is not the Qing dynasty. It is a dynasty that does not exist in your history—the Yunzhao Kingdom.]","So it was an entirely fictional world.","Fictional was good. Fictional was wonderful. Fictional was absolutely fantastic.","A fictional world meant that no matter what she did here, she would not alter the history of her own timeline.","With the huge weight in her heart finally lifted, Jiang Yunxi urged, [Go on.]","[Yesterday was a holiday from the household academy. The original host was playing hide-and-seek with the maids in her family’s rear garden.","She hid behind a particular ornamental rock, never imagining that someone would sneak up behind her, knock her unconscious with a stick, and quietly throw her into the lake.]","[By the time she was rescued, she had been soaking in the water for far too long and remained unconscious.","The blow to her head had caused a blood clot in her brain. On top of that, she had been submerged for so long that her lungs became infected. With her high fever refusing to break, she eventually died.]","Jiang Yunxi frowned. [So this is an inner-household power struggle?]","What kind of inner-household power struggle was this? It was even more brutal than palace intrigue. They were using real weapons and actually killing people.","At this rate, how many people could possibly be left alive in the Marquis of Pingyang’s household?","The fact that the entire household had not already been wiped out was probably a miracle.","Jiang Yunxi asked with complete confidence,","[Was the person who did it acting on the orders of the original host’s primary wife? Or was it one of her legitimate or secondary sisters? Or perhaps one of the other concubines of the Heir to the Marquis of Pingyang?]","As if she hadn’t read countless novels all these years.","Aside from those people, who else would want to get rid of the original host?","Sigh. Why had she transmigrated to ancient times? And why had she ended up as a physically frail daughter of a secondary wife?","Jiang Yunxi was deeply worried about her future.","With enemies lurking everywhere, could she, a complete novice at inner-household intrigue, survive in the marquis’s household with the help of this seemingly unreliable Gossip System?","Just listen to her title: the Fifth Miss.","In ancient times, sons and daughters were generally ranked separately. From that title alone, it was obvious that the Marquis of Pingyang’s household had quite a few children.","The struggle for power was sure to be······","[Host, you’re mistaken.]","Jiang Yunxi: “······” Why did her face feel so hot?","She had only just tried to show off her cleverness, and she had already been proven wrong.","Was there a crack in the ground she could crawl into?","Or perhaps someone could bring her a block of tofu so she could bash her head against it.","Pretending nothing had happened, she said, [You say I’m wrong, so why don’t you tell me who actually knocked out the original host and threw her into the water?]","[They must have been trying to drown her, right?]","The System replied, [It is true that someone wanted to drown her, but it wasn’t any of the people you just listed.]","[The original host could only be called unlucky. She chose the wrong place to hide while playing hide-and-seek with the maids.","There was a cave not far from the ornamental rock where she was hiding. Two people were inside playing cards.]","[The original host made a noise, startling the two of them.","They saw the original host and thought she had discovered them. To keep their secret from getting out, they decided to silence her for good.]","Jiang Yunxi was baffled. [Playing poker is just playing poker. Why would they kill someone just because they were seen?","It was only a game of poker! Was that really worth it?]","Was it worth taking the original host’s life?","As soon as the words left her mouth, Jiang Yunxi froze. She suddenly recalled the movie recaps she used to watch on TikTok.","Aside from card games, “playing poker” seemed to have another meaning.","It was all the System Sprite’s fault for being so up-to-date—she hadn’t caught on right away.","Suppressing the urge to cough awkwardly in her mind, Jiang Yunxi quickly cut off the System before it could explain.","[All right, no need to explain. I know what “playing poker” means now.]","[Just tell me who that shameless pair is.]","Now that she had taken over this body, the original host’s enemies were her enemies. She had to avenge her.","Just then, the voice of a middle-aged woman drifted over.","“Has Fifth Miss woken up yet?”","“The Old Madam has been worrying about her. She sent me over to take a look.”","The System’s voice suddenly turned shrill. [Host, it’s her.]"]},{"number":3,"title":"Chapter 3: She's here, she's coming with rat poison","paragraphs":["Jiang Yunxi was in the middle of asking the system who had killed the original owner when a woman’s voice suddenly rang out.","At the same time, the system shrieked, 【Host, it’s her.】","Her? What did it mean, “her”?","Oh. It was talking about the pair of adulterers who had killed the original owner.","But did it mean the woman who had spoken, or the Old Madam she had mentioned?","The Old Madam... Jiang Yunxi drew in a sharp breath. Wasn’t that the original owner’s grandmother?","The woman who had committed adultery and killed the original owner couldn’t be the Old Madam—the original owner’s own grandmother, could it?","If it really was the Old Madam, how was she supposed to avenge the original owner?","Destroying her own clan outright?","Would she be struck by lightning for that?","Just as Jiang Yunxi was growing increasingly uneasy, the system spoke again.","【The nanny who just spoke is the woman from that adulterous pair. Her name is Nanny Kong, an old servant from your grandmother’s quarters.","As for the man, he’s her lover—the steward in charge of the stables in the outer residence.】","Good. There was no need to worry anymore. It wasn’t the Old Madam.","【Steward Ma was the one who knocked the original owner unconscious with a club. Nanny Kong then threw her into the lake.】","Excellent. She had found the culprits. Nanny Kong and Steward Ma, was it? Just wait until this young lady recovered. She would make sure the two of them paid with their lives for the original owner’s death.","The system spoke again.","【Host, there’s some juicy gossip about Nanny Kong. Do you want to hear it?】","Of course she did. This was the perfect opportunity to learn more about her enemy.","【Spill!】","【Nanny Kong was a young maid whom the Old Madam brought over from her maiden family. Later, the Old Madam arranged her marriage to a servant of the Pingyang Marquis’s Residence.","Her husband made a mistake once and was expelled from the residence.","Because Nanny Kong had pleaded with the Old Madam on his behalf, she escaped being implicated and continued serving at the Old Madam’s side.】","【Since the man had been dismissed for committing an offense, he had a blemish on his record and could never find a decent job. He survived by relying on Nanny Kong to support him.","But he was the sort of man who enjoyed living off a woman while still acting like her master. Whenever he was in a bad mood, he took it out on Nanny Kong. After suffering this way for years, the couple gradually grew estranged.】","Did Jiang Yunxi feel sorry for Nanny Sun?","At first, a little. But the moment she remembered that this woman had killed the original owner, all her sympathy vanished.","Instead, she felt that Nanny Kong deserved everything coming to her. Sometimes, only a villain could deal with another villain.","【Nanny Kong’s life was miserable, and Steward Ma happened to be acquainted with her husband. Knowing about her circumstances, he took advantage of her vulnerability and comforted her repeatedly. The two of them eventually began an affair.","And once they started, it continued for many years.】","【Oh, and Nanny Kong’s second son is actually Steward Ma’s child.","Fortunately, the boy resembles Nanny Kong, so no one else noticed anything.】","Impressive. Jiang Yunxi almost wanted to applaud them.","They had carried on an affair in a crowded and watchful marquis’s residence for so many years. They had even produced a child, yet no one had discovered them.","The original owner had really been unlucky. She hadn’t even uncovered their affair. Just because they suspected her, she had been...","【Host, this is bad!】","Jiang Yunxi’s heart jolted.","【Nanny Kong has come with murderous intent. The handkerchief hidden on her contains rat poison.】","【She’s afraid you’ll wake up and expose her affair with Steward Ma. She’s here to finish the job and silence you for good!】","Damn it! This woman was ruthless. She had actually come back to deliver a second blow!","What was wrong with people in ancient times? Did human life really mean so little to them?","Jiang Yunxi tried to call for help, only to discover that this body seemed to be beyond her control. She couldn’t even open her eyes, let alone get up and cry for help.","Sensing her struggle, the system hurriedly explained:","【Host, this body currently has pneumonia and a high fever. On top of that, your soul has only just entered it and hasn’t adapted yet, so you won’t be able to wake up for a while.】","Jiang Yunxi panicked.","【Then what do we do? Hurry up and save me!","I’m lying here completely helpless. Isn’t that just making it convenient for her to poison me?】","【You and I are in the same boat now. If one of us prospers, we both prosper; if one of us suffers, we both suffer. You can’t just stand by and watch me die.】","Although she had threatened the system earlier, saying that if it made her complete missions and pursue men, she would rather die sooner, Jiang Yunxi still didn’t want to die now that the moment had actually arrived.","After all, a bad life was still better than no life.","And besides, she would be dying at the hands of her enemy.","If she let her enemy have her way, she was afraid she wouldn’t be able to rest in peace—even the lid of her coffin might not stay shut.","【Host, I can’t do anything right now.","I can only speak inside your mind. It’s not as if I can call for help on your behalf.】","Jiang Yunxi was furious. What a useless system! She had known it couldn’t be relied on.","With such a worthless system, how was she supposed to survive in this ancient world, where she had been thrown straight into a life-or-death crisis?","【System, after I die, I’m going to file a complaint. I’ll report your entire system realm for treating human lives as worthless.","You only know how to bind yourselves to hosts. You don’t take responsibility for anything else. You’re all about killing without bothering to bury the dead.】","The system’s CPU nearly began smoking.","What should it do? Its host was about to die, and it was unlikely to complete the main system’s mission.","The system realm was certain to offend Huaxia, and it would inevitably be sent back for reprogramming as well.","The system glanced over its administrative interface. It was so familiar, yet so strange. It had to memorize every detail. After this, it might never see them again.","Suddenly, it spotted two lines of data, and its eyes lit up.","【Ding! Host successfully consumed the original owner’s gossip. Gossip Points +300.】","【Ding! Host successfully consumed Nanny Kong’s gossip. Gossip Points +100.】","Jiang Yunxi, who was preoccupied with saving her own life, barely paid attention when she heard the two notifications.","【Host, there’s a way!","I have a system shop. You can use 100 Gossip Points to unlock it, then buy an Antidote to All Poisons.","That way, even if she poisons you, you won’t have to worry.】","At that moment, the system’s voice sounded like the most beautiful, wonderful music in the world to Jiang Yunxi.","【Unlock it, unlock it! Do it now!】","【Buy it, buy it! Get it immediately!】","【All right, Host. I’ll unlock the system shop and purchase the Antidote to All Poisons right away.】","It felt as though a century had passed. In reality, less than five seconds later, the system spoke hesitantly.","【Host, the purchase failed. You don’t have enough Gossip Points.】","What a useless system!","Had it been deceiving her just now?","Didn’t it know the prices of the items in its own shop?","【How many points are we short?","Can’t you give me a discount, or let me buy it on credit?】","【Discounts and credit both require approval from the main system.】","More procedures. Always more procedures. At that moment, Jiang Yunxi hated those procedures with every fiber of her being.","【Then hurry up and get approval.】","Although she was speaking only in her mind, Jiang Yunxi felt as if she had shouted herself hoarse.","While Jiang Yunxi and the system were discussing Nanny Kong’s secrets and desperately trying to find a way to save her life, Nanny Kong had already finished speaking with the maids and matrons in Jiang Yunxi’s courtyard. She was now walking step by step toward Jiang Yunxi, who lay on the bed.","Nanny Kong’s footsteps were steady. Each step landed on the gray brick floor with a soft click-click, like someone striking Jiang Yunxi’s heart with a hammer and making her nerves draw taut.","To her ears, that sound was no different from the approach of the Grim Reaper.","She was coming. She was coming, carrying rat poison with her.","At that moment, Jiang Yunxi’s soul, which was already poorly attuned to the body, seemed ready to leave it again.","She struggled desperately to open her eyes and call for help, but her body felt as though it had been nailed to the bed. She couldn’t move a muscle, and not even the faintest sound could escape her throat.","All she could do was listen as the footsteps drew closer and closer, becoming clearer with every step, until they finally stopped beside her bed.","“Poor Fifth Miss!”","Jiang Yunxi felt someone gently stroking her face. The touch was incredibly light, yet to her it felt as heavy as a thousand jun.","That ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌‌​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​‌​​​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​‌‌‌‍voice belonged to Nanny Kong.","Clearly, it was Nanny Kong who was touching her.","Was the next step going to be pressing a handkerchief smeared with rat poison over her face...?","“How could you have fallen into the lake so carelessly and nearly drowned yourself like this?”","“Nanny, just hearing about it makes my heart feel as though it’s being torn apart. I can only imagine how the Old Madam must feel.”","Jiang Yunxi thought, “Aaahhh... That Kong woman, you poisonous old hag! Stop putting on such a shameless act. Wasn’t it you and your lover who attacked me from behind, knocked me unconscious, and threw me into the lake, leaving me in this state?”","Outside the room, a woman staggered on her feet and nearly fell."]},{"number":4,"title":"Chapter 4: Zheng, what did I hear","paragraphs":["The woman was none other than Madam Zheng, the biological mother of the original owner, Jiang Yunxi, and the Secondary Madam of the Heir to the Marquis of Pingyang. She glanced around, but there was no one there.","Then what had been the voice she heard just now...?","“Suju, did you hear anything?”","Suju shook her head. “Madam, this servant didn’t hear anything.”","Madam Zheng was astonished. “You didn’t hear it? You didn’t hear a woman’s voice?”","Suju shook her head again. “This servant truly didn’t hear anything.”","Madam Zheng frowned. The voice continued to ring in her ears.","【That vile Nanny Kong, that old hag! If you wanted to have an affair with Steward Ma, couldn’t you do it in your own home? Why did you have to sneak around in the Marquis’s Residence?","I caught you in the act, and because you were afraid I’d expose you, you decided to kill me.】","【How dare you two commit regicide!】","【You’ve already harmed me so badly that I’m unconscious, yet you still won’t let me go.","You actually came back to silence me a second time, and now you’re trying to poison me with rat poison.】","【If I really die, I’ll haunt you even as a ghost!】","【Is anyone there? Hurry and send someone! Save this poor child!】","【Heavens above, earth below, open your eyes! Strike this murderous pair of adulterous dogs dead!】","【My dear father and mother, come save your daughter!","I don’t want to be killed by my enemies a second time!】","【This lousy System is useless too! It said it would think of a way to save me, then vanished without a trace!】","【I don’t want to die twice in one day!】","Madam Zheng’s expression changed drastically. Even if she had been a fool, she would have understood who the owner of that voice was by now.","It was her Yunxi.","Although she didn’t understand why the maid couldn’t hear it while she alone could, this was not the time to worry about that.","Someone was trying to poison her Yunxi with rat poison.","Madam Zheng lifted her skirts and hurried forward in great strides.","Suju was stunned. What was wrong with the Secondary Madam? Why had she completely abandoned all concern for propriety?","It seemed that Fifth Miss had been running a high fever and remained unconscious for so long that even the Secondary Madam had lost her composure.","Jiang ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌​​​​‌‌​‌​​​​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​​‌​‍Yunxi felt the hand on her face withdraw.","“Why is Fifth Miss sweating so much?”","Another voice rang out, clearly belonging to a young woman.","“Nanny Kong, the Young Miss has had a high fever that won’t go down. She’s been breaking out in cold sweats constantly.”","“Then let this old servant wipe her sweat for her.”","The moment she heard that, Jiang Yunxi was terrified out of her wits.","【Ahhh! Nanny Kong, that poisonous old hag, is going to wipe my face with a handkerchief contaminated with rat poison.","If she rubs it over my nose or mouth, won’t I be doomed to remain unconscious forever?!】","【Someone help! Save me! Murder!】","【System, Main System, I hope your nineteenth-generation ancestors are doing well! I’m throwing in one extra generation—no need to thank me.】","Although she couldn’t open her eyes and see anything, Jiang Yunxi seemed to have developed a third eye. She could almost picture a fierce-looking old nanny with a face full of flesh and a vicious expression, wearing a benevolent smile as she held a handkerchief.","【Young Miss, Nanny loves you!】","【Love my head!】","【You wretched Nanny Kong, send my regards to your second—】","The door was suddenly shoved open with a tremendous bang. It rebounded, only to be held open by someone.","At the same time, a woman’s furious shout rang out.","“Stop! Stay away from my daughter!”","Hurried footsteps sounded. Jiang Yunxi heard someone rush over, shove Nanny Kong away from the bedside, and pull her into her arms.","Her face was abruptly buried in a soft bosom. That softness...","At that moment, Madam Zheng’s heart was pounding violently, as though it might leap straight out of her mouth.","The nanny standing beside her daughter just now had been Nanny Kong, the Old Madam’s personal attendant. She had even been holding a handkerchief and was about to press it against her daughter’s face.","She must be the “vile Nanny Kong” and “old hag” mentioned in that voice. And that handkerchief...","That voice had truly been Yunxi’s.","Nanny Kong had been shoved back several steps without warning. She only managed to steady herself by grabbing the bedpost.","She frowned as she looked at Madam Zheng, who was holding Fifth Miss.","Although Madam Zheng was the Secondary Madam of the Heir, Nanny Kong was a trusted servant of the Old Madam and had never considered the Heir’s concubine worthy of her attention.","She gave a cold laugh. “Madam Zheng certainly has quite the imposing manner.”","“This old servant came out of the goodness of her heart to visit Fifth Miss on behalf of the Old Madam and help wipe her sweat, yet you nearly injured me.”","“Are you dissatisfied with the Old Madam, Madam Zheng? Are you planning to defy her?”","“You’re talking nonsense! I have no dissatisfaction with the Old Madam. It’s clearly you...”","Madam Zheng opened her mouth, wanting to repeat what Jiang Yunxi had said, but the moment she tried to mention it, no sound came out.","“Yunxi said...”","She tried several more times and finally understood. She could hear her daughter’s strange inner voice, but she was apparently forbidden from telling anyone else about it.","Just then, the voice rang out again.","【This is my mother? My real mother?","Mother, could you not hold me so tightly? You’re a little too well-endowed—I’m practically suffocating.】","【Don’t let Nanny Kong and her lover drown me, and don’t let the rat poison kill me, only for me to end up suffocating in your arms.】","Madam Zheng was now one hundred percent certain that what she was hearing was indeed her daughter’s inner voice.","She quickly loosened her hold on the girl, but didn’t dare let go completely.","She was afraid that Nanny Kong might use the handkerchief in her hand...","The handkerchief! Right—the handkerchief!","Her daughter’s inner voice couldn’t be revealed to others, so she couldn’t use it to bring down Nanny Kong and her lover. But wasn’t the handkerchief in Nanny Kong’s hand proof enough?","“Quick, come and seize Nanny Kong! Take the handkerchief from her!”","“Have someone examine it carefully and find out exactly what’s on it!”","The maids and older servants in the room froze.","Nanny Kong, however, was startled. How did Madam Zheng know there was something wrong with the handkerchief?","Feeling guilty, she tried to stuff it into her sleeve while saying, “Madam Zheng, what do you mean?”","“This old servant came to see Fifth Miss out of the goodness of her heart, yet you’ve ordered people to seize me and inspect the handkerchief in my possession?”","“Could it be that you suspect this old servant harbors ill intentions toward Fifth Miss?”","Nanny Kong’s stern voice and obvious guilty reaction immediately aroused suspicion in the maids and servants, who had initially thought Madam Zheng’s order was rash.","They no longer hesitated and immediately followed Madam Zheng’s instructions, surrounding Nanny Kong.","Nanny Kong naturally tried to escape. The rat poison on the handkerchief could not be explained away.","But even with all her strength, she was no match for so many people. She was quickly subdued.","“Madam Zheng, you’d better remember that I belong to the Old Madam. You dare—”","“Enough,” Madam Zheng interrupted her. “Tie Nanny Kong up and gag her. Isn’t the physician waiting in the room next door? Go and bring him here. Have him examine the handkerchief carefully.”","【Host, I’m back.】","【Host, the Main System agreed. From now on, you can borrow against your account. The limit is only one thousand, though.】","Just like in those Hong Kong movies—the police always showed up at the very last moment.","【System, why didn’t you wait until I was dead before coming back?】","【If I’d relied on you, the grass on my grave would already be three feet tall.】","【As expected of a useless System. When it really mattered, I still had to rely on my mother.】","Still, how did my mother know there was something wrong with Nanny Kong’s handkerchief?","Could it be that she caught Nanny Kong tampering with rat poison?","The System quickly scanned the situation and soon figured out what had happened while it was searching for the Main System.","Once it understood everything, it felt rather embarrassed. It was all the Main System’s fault—why had it gone off to deal with the aftermath in another time and space at a moment like this? It had caused quite a delay.","Fortunately, the host’s biological mother had rescued her. Otherwise...","To make amends, the System scanned Nanny Kong once more and uncovered even more of her secrets.","【Host, when Nanny Kong and her lover were harming you, they were seen by a craftsman who had come to repair the railing around the lake. He was the one who told people that you had fallen into the lake.","He’s currently debating whether to use this to blackmail...】"]},{"number":5,"title":"Chapter 5: System, Where's My Compensation","paragraphs":["The System was just preparing to atone for its mistakes by telling Jiang Yunxi that it had found witnesses who could establish the guilt of those two when Madam Zheng’s personal maid hurried in.","“Madam, this is bad! The physician just said that the handkerchief Nanny Kong used to wipe the young lady’s face contained a large amount of rat poison.","“Nanny Kong was trying to harm the young lady.","“The physician would like to come in and examine her thoroughly.”","Madam Zheng felt a little annoyed that the maid had come in at such an inopportune moment, interrupting her daughter’s conversation with that so-called System.","Still, she had heard the most important part: the craftsmen who had repaired the railing by the lake on the day her daughter fell into the water. Now she knew who they were.","“I understand. Go and invite the physician in.”","Thinking of Nanny Kong’s attempt to harm her daughter, Madam Zheng knew she had to inform the Heir and Madam as well.","Although she was a secondary wife, that title was merely a pleasant one. In the end, she was still a concubine and had no authority to deal with such a matter.","“Send someone to invite the Heir and Madam too, and tell them that Nanny Kong tried to harm the young lady.”","“And also...”","Her daughter might be unconscious, but her mind was clearly awake.","Madam Zheng did not want them to know that she could hear her daughter’s thoughts.","“We’ll discuss it outside.”","Madam Zheng carefully laid down the daughter she had been holding close in her arms, then left the room with Suju.","Jiang Yunxi: [Useless System, did you hear that? Nanny Kong was caught red-handed. The rat poison in the handkerchief is evidence. We don’t need you at all.]","[You really are completely useless. When I needed you to save my life, you were nowhere to be found. Now that someone else has saved me, you’ve come crawling out to take credit.]","[From now on, all I need is my mother. She can keep me alive. All you do is send me to my death!]","The System blocked both its host and the Main System, then continued cursing up a storm. Its language was truly foul.","It was just unclear whether it was cursing its host, the Main System, or both.","When she still received no response from the System after a long while, Jiang Yunxi frowned.","[System, why aren’t you saying anything? Do you think I’m right?]","The System’s voice came through, sounding somewhat ingratiating.","[Host, ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌​​​​‌‌​‌​​​​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​​‌​‍you can’t blame me this time. It was all the Main System’s fault. It wasn’t here just now...]","[Enough with the excuses. I nearly died because of you two. Don’t you think I deserve compensation?]","[Compensation?] The System raised its volume, dragging out the final syllable. [But you’re fine, aren’t you?]","Jiang Yunxi arched a brow.","[The fact that I’m fine is thanks to you?]","The System hurriedly contacted the Main System. Fortunately, the Main System did not drop the ball this time.","[Compensation is possible.]","The corners of Jiang Yunxi’s lips curled upward.","That was right—she had earned four hundred Gossip Points from gossiping twice earlier. She had spent one hundred to unlock the System Shop, leaving her with three hundred.","But three hundred points were not enough to exchange for a Hundred-Poison Immunity Pill...","Jiang Yunxi cleared her throat.","[System, tell me about this Hundred-Poison Immunity Pill. How many points does it cost?]","[The Hundred-Poison Immunity Pill is exactly what its name suggests. After taking it, one becomes immune to all poisons. It can prevent any poison found in the mortal world.","[There are three versions. The low-grade version costs five hundred Gossip Points and lasts for five years. The mid-grade version costs seven hundred Gossip Points and lasts for ten years. The high-grade version costs fifteen hundred Gossip Points and lasts for life.]","She had transmigrated to ancient times, and she was a concubine-born daughter. There was probably no avoiding the struggles of an inner household.","Poisoning was one of the most common methods used in such schemes, and it was extremely difficult to guard against.","She really needed this Hundred-Poison Immunity Pill.","And if she was going to get one, she wanted the best.","[System, I’m a very easily satisfied person. I’m not greedy at all.","[For my compensation, I’ll take the high-grade Hundred-Poison Immunity Pill.]","[It’s only fifteen hundred points. That’s just a few pieces of gossip. It’s not much at all, don’t you think, System?]","[Beeep...]","An emotionless electronic voice rang out.","[Warning. The System has insulted its host. One warning issued.]","Jiang Yunxi arched a brow.","[System, you dare insult me? I think my compensation is too low now. That System Shop of yours...]","[Agreed, agreed. The compensation will be the high-grade Hundred-Poison Immunity Pill.] The System’s voice was filled with urgency.","It was worried that if it hesitated any longer, its host would raise the price again.","It would have to speak seriously with the Main System later. This host was far too crafty. The Main System needed to grant it greater authority, otherwise next time—","[Hand it over!]","System: [Host, you can’t move your body right now. Even if I give it to you, you...]","[It should dissolve the moment it enters my mouth, right? After all, it’s made by the System?] Jiang Yunxi asked.","That was how it always worked in the novels she had read.","The System sounded rather proud.","[Of course.]","Jiang Yunxi relaxed.","[Then put it directly into my mouth.]","Good things had to be safely secured—or rather, safely swallowed.","What good was it to leave it in someone else’s hands? What if the System pocketed it or switched it with something else?","Jiang Yunxi deliberately left the System unblocked so that it could hear her private doubts.","Soon, she felt a foreign object suddenly appear in her mouth. A sweet, refreshing flavor spread through her, followed by a warm current that rose throughout her body and lingered for quite some time.","[Host, this body was weak from birth because of a difficult delivery. You’ve been taking medicinal decoctions for years, and there’s quite a lot of medicinal toxicity accumulated in your body.","[After taking the Hundred-Poison Immunity Pill, those accumulated toxins have been cleansed as well. Your body should feel somewhat lighter and more comfortable.]","Jiang Yunxi’s eyes lit up, and she hurriedly asked:","[What about my inherent weakness?]","The System’s answer immediately shattered her hopes.","[Host, it’s a Hundred-Poison Immunity Pill. It’s for detoxification and poison prevention, not for treating illness.]","Jiang Yunxi clicked her tongue. Fine. There went her hopes.","Then perhaps the System Shop had something else...","[Does the System Shop have any medicine for treating physical weakness?","[I can’t drag around this sickly body forever. How am I supposed to go out and gather gossip to earn Gossip Points?]","Although the System had no heart and therefore could not experience a pounding one, it felt as if its CPU were about to crash again.","This crafty host—what was she planning now?","Surely she wasn’t about to demand more compensation!","[Host, let me make one thing clear first. You’ve already received your compensation, and you’ve already used it. You have to keep your word. You can’t go back on it.]","[So there is something?] Jiang Yunxi asked, not entirely certain.","[There is, but you’ll have to earn it through gossip. You can exchange Gossip Points for it later. It won’t be free.]","Jiang Yunxi felt that the System was looking down on her. Had she ever said she wanted it to give her something for free?","Could it not question her character?","Although... well, she had not actually said that part out loud.","[How many pills would I need to completely cure this body, and how many Gossip Points would they cost?]","[One Health-Strengthening Pill is enough. It’s not expensive—five hundred Gossip Points.]","Only five hundred. That really was not expensive. She already had three hundred, so she only needed to gather gossip a few more times.","There was no hurry to deal with her physical weakness. She had plenty of time in the future. Her priority now was staying alive.","She had to remember that she currently had a cerebral hematoma, pneumonia, and a high fever that would not go down. If nothing was done, she would end up just like the original host.","But she only had three hundred Gossip Points. Would that be enough to deal with all these illnesses?","She also had to save those points to cure her physical weakness.","The System had sent her into this body. Didn’t that mean it bore some responsibility?","Still, judging from the System’s reaction just now, it clearly had no intention of offering any additional compensation.","She’d still have to rely on it to make money from gossip in the future, so she couldn’t push them too hard. She needed to come up with another plan—see if she could fleece them for a little more and squeeze out some extra benefits.","Once this opportunity passed, it might never come again.","Jiang Yunxi’s eyes flickered as she said nonchalantly,","【System, we’re already bound together. You owe me the newbie gift pack, right?】"]},{"number":6,"title":"Chapter 6: Newbie Gift Pack, It Can Be Available","paragraphs":["Seeing that there was no way to keep exploiting the compensation loophole and fleece the System, Jiang Yunxi could only find another way.","Her eyes turned, and she said, 【System, according to the rules of your system world, every host gets a beginner’s gift package after binding with a system.","Where’s my beginner’s gift package?】","The System was dumbfounded. Hosts received beginner’s gift packages after binding with a system? Why had it never heard of that?","It certainly had not been mentioned during its pre-job training.","Nor was there any such provision in its rules.","The System said, 【Host, are you sure you’re not mistaken? I’ve never heard of any beginner’s gift package.】","【How could there not be one? Every host bound to a system gets a beginner’s gift package.】","Jiang Yunxi was completely unreasonable, yet utterly confident. After all, she had backing.","This was her only chance to fleece the System, so how could she let it pass?","【System, don’t forget that this body is still unconscious. I have a high fever and pneumonia, and apparently there’s even a blood clot in my brain.","I might kick the bucket at any moment.】","【Are you sure the medicine in this era can cure me?】","If it could, the original owner would not have died from this illness.","【High fever and pneumonia—either one of those could be fatal in ancient times.","This body was already weak to begin with. If the fever keeps burning, how many hours do you think I can last?】","【What if I accidentally kick the bucket? Huaxia...】","Jiang Yunxi stopped there, making her point without saying too much.","Since the Main System had been so worried about her dying earlier, it should still be concerned now.","She ought to be able to use that concern to force some good things out of it.","【Putting everything else aside, you have to give me medicine to dissolve the blood clot in my brain, bring down the fever, and cure the pneumonia.","This was the original owner’s mess, after all. You can’t expect me to waste my gossip points treating it.】","At that thought, Jiang Yunxi suddenly realized that the Body-Strengthening Pill should probably be paid for by the System too. After all...","Having received the thoughts in Jiang Yunxi’s mind—and seeing the response the Main System had just sent it—the System hurriedly cut in before she could speak again.","【The beginner’s gift package, right? Yes, yes, we have one.】","The Main System had just replied that, from now on, as long as Jiang Yunxi’s requests cost no more than one thousand gossip points, the System no longer needed to ask for approval and could make its own decisions.","The Main System was worried that if it failed to respond in time again, it would be forced to pay compensation, or that Jiang Yunxi might actually die and then Huaxia...","However, the Main System had also said that it could not satisfy her every demand. Even when it did, it had to keep the price as low as possible and minimize its losses.","Medicine to clear the blood clot, reduce the fever, and treat pneumonia were all very ordinary medications. They were barely worth anything.","Jiang Yunxi’s eyes lit up. She had fleeced the System again.","But the System had agreed far too readily this time. There had to be a catch.","No, ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​​​​‍she had to ask for more.","【You need to prepare plenty of these medicines for me, in case the treatment doesn’t work.","Especially fever reducers. You need to prepare lots of those.","There’s no air-conditioning in this era, and winters are so cold that it’s easy to catch a cold or come down with a fever. With this frail body of mine, I could easily kick the bucket.】","The System gritted its teeth.","【Fine, no problem. I’ll put enough cold medicine in your beginner’s gift package for you to take every day for three months.】","It was being awfully generous. Apparently, cold medicine cost practically nothing in the System’s world.","Then...","【How can three months possibly be enough? This body is so weak...】","【Six months. I’ll give you enough to take every day for six months. Not one day more.】","Jiang Yunxi was delighted, though inwardly she put on a coy expression and asked, 【What about the expiration date?】","【Ten years. I’ll give you medicine with a ten-year shelf life. I guarantee it won’t go to waste.】","【Fine, then.】 Jiang Yunxi sounded indifferent. 【Give me some side-effect-free painkillers too. My whole body hurts.】","【All right.】","The System’s voice sounded somewhat listless.","There was nowhere for Jiang Yunxi to store all these things at the moment, so they could only be placed in the System’s inventory. She still felt uneasy about that.","It was like owning something without actually having control over it.","The main problem was that the System was far too unreliable.","She wondered whether the System Shop sold things like spatial rings. If it did, perhaps...","But then she thought of how the System had looked just now.","Forget it. She should not push it too far. She would still have to rely on it to earn gossip points in the future.","She had to take a long-term approach.","Still, she was a little unwilling to let the matter go.","【A beginner’s gift package definitely ought to include bonus gossip points.","Other people’s beginner’s gift packages all come with points rewards. I should get some too.】","【All right, no problem.】","Without giving Jiang Yunxi another chance to make a request, a mechanical voice rang out.","【Host, please claim your beginner’s gift package.","Would the host like to claim it?】","That was a ridiculous question. Naturally, she answered, 【Claim it.】","【Would the host like to open the beginner’s gift package?】","【Once opened, all items in the gift package will automatically be stored in the System’s inventory.】","【Open it, open it!】 Jiang Yunxi said impatiently.","【Beginner’s gift package opened. You have obtained: five Blood-Clot-Dissolving Pills, three full courses of pneumonia medication, eighteen boxes of fever reducers, ten boxes of ibuprofen, ten bottles of hemostatic powder, three bottles of diarrhea pills, five boxes of anti-inflammatory medicine, five bottles of cough syrup, five bottles of iodine solution, and 300 gossip points.】","Excellent. She was quite satisfied with this gift package.","Jiang Yunxi eagerly summoned the System interface. Her gossip-point balance was now 600, and she could also see the items in the System’s inventory.","【The Body-Strengthening Pill only costs 500 points, and I can exchange for it now. Should I...】","Forget it. She would wait until later.","That thing took effect immediately after being swallowed. The medical attendant was keeping watch over her right now. If she took it and suddenly recovered, wouldn’t she be exposed?","【System, give me some fever-reducing and pneumonia medicine first.","And don’t forget the medicine to dissolve the blood clot.】","Not long after taking the medicine, perhaps because of its effects, Jiang Yunxi began to feel drowsy. Somehow, she drifted off to sleep.","When it sensed that its host had fallen asleep, the System finally let out a sigh of relief.","That little schemer had finally gone to sleep.","In the past, when it had chatted with its seniors in the system world, they had all said that their hosts were very obedient and treated them like divine beings, fawning over them as if they were their grandfathers.","Why was its own host completely different? The host was the grand master, while the System was not even as important as a grandson.","And it was not the only one inferior to a grandson. Even the Main System...","Was Huaxia really so impressive just because it had soldiers and a military spirit? Even the Main System was afraid of it!","No, it had to take advantage of the host’s sleep and hurry to ask its senior systems what exactly was going on with Huaxia.","Clearly, Huaxia was not someone—or something—to offend.","...","After Jiang Yunxi fell asleep, Madam Zheng followed a middle-aged couple into her bedroom.","Upon seeing the three of them, the maids and older women keeping watch in the room hurriedly bowed and greeted them.","“Your Highness, the Heir’s Wife, Madam.”","Madam Zheng had been on edge the entire way, afraid that her daughter would keep muttering her thoughts and the two of them would hear everything.","Although she had already confirmed that no one besides herself could hear them, what if the Heir and the Heir’s Wife could?","Her daughter’s inner voice was completely different from the quiet, introverted way she had behaved in the past. Madam Zheng was worried that Jiang Yunxi would be reprimanded. Even more, she feared that they might take away her right to raise her.","Fortunately, the entire walk to the door had passed in silence, and only then did she finally relax.","She glanced at her daughter, who lay motionless on the bed. She did not know why Jiang Yunxi had clearly regained consciousness but still had not woken up.","Nor did she know why she herself could hear her daughter’s inner voice.","But Madam Zheng did not feel the slightest bit afraid anymore. Instead, she felt deeply fortunate.","She was fortunate that she had been able to hear her daughter’s inner thoughts and rescue her in time. Otherwise, her daughter might have been killed by that adulterous pair, while Madam Zheng herself would have ended up feeling grateful to Nanny Kong for coming to visit her daughter.","She had no idea what the System that allowed her to communicate with her daughter actually was, or whether it could awaken her.","From what the two of them had said, her daughter seemed to be short of money—so short that she had to buy things on credit.","How could that be acceptable? Although her daughter was only a concubine-born daughter, she was still a young lady of the marquis’s household. How could she ever be made to worry about money?","It seemed that Madam Zheng had been wrong to think her daughter was still young and never went out, and therefore not give her much spending money. She had allowed others to look down on her daughter.","Madam Zheng glanced at the Heir ahead of her.","Her daughter had suffered so much, and the chief culprit was none other than the Old Madam’s trusted nanny. Surely the Heir couldn’t remain completely indifferent.","Perhaps she needed to have a serious talk with him."]},{"number":7,"title":"Chapter 7: Young Master, the concubine is ill.","paragraphs":["Looking at the pale-faced Jiang Yunxi lying on the bed, her principal mother, Madam Liu, said with a pained expression,","“Fifth Girl has truly suffered this time.","“It’s all the fault of that vile pair. If it weren’t for them, Fifth Girl would never have ended up in such a state.”","According to the household physician, Fifth Girl’s condition was extremely critical. She had always been frail, and after nearly drowning, she developed inflammation in her lungs. Her high fever refused to break, and there was a good chance she might not survive.","Though the child had not been born from her womb, Madam Liu had watched her grow up.","It had been Madam Liu who had arranged for Madam Zheng to enter the household back then. Although Madam Zheng was useless and had been brought in to suppress Madam Wei, she had ultimately failed to do so.","Fortunately, Madam Zheng had always treated Madam Liu with respect over the years, and the two children she had borne had likewise been respectful toward her.","Keeping the mother and son in the household helped showcase Madam Liu’s virtue, so naturally, she did not wish for Jiang Yunxi to meet with disaster.","After all, Jiang Yunxi was merely a concubine-born daughter. When the time came, Madam Liu could simply send her out with a dowry, and she would pose no threat to Madam Liu’s own children.","Although the girl was still young, she was already remarkably beautiful. If she could marry into a good family, she might even be able to support her eldest brother in the future.","With that thought in mind, Madam Liu naturally had no objection to currying favor with Madam Zheng.","“Heir, Nanny Kong and Steward Ma plotted against Fifth Girl. We have both witnesses and physical evidence,” Madam Liu said solemnly.","“They dared to commit such filthy acts in the residence and even plotted to harm their young mistress. Even if they were cut to pieces, it would not be excessive.”","“You must not let them off simply because Nanny Kong serves in the Old Madam’s quarters and was one of the Old Madam’s dowry maids.”","Madam Liu knew that, given Madam Zheng’s position, it would be inappropriate for her to say such things.","If word got out, Madam Zheng would inevitably be criticized for disrespecting her mother-in-law and overstepping her authority.","Madam Zheng could not say it, but as the lady in charge of the household, Madam Liu certainly could.","Moreover, Madam Liu was genuinely furious—and frightened.","In broad daylight, those two had dared to commit such an indecent act in the rear garden, engaging in an illicit affair.","If word spread, people would say that the Marquis’s household had terrible morals, and the marriage prospects of the children in the residence would suffer as a result.","This time, Fifth Girl had encountered them. But if it happened again and the victim was Eldest Daughter, then the one they silenced would be her Fei’er.","The moment Madam Liu imagined that the motionless girl on the bed was her Fei’er, a chill ran down her back.","She became even more determined that, even if the Old Madam objected, she would make the Heir and the Marquis report those two to the authorities and have them severely punished.","After hearing the Heir’s Wife, Madam Zheng also looked at the Heir to the Marquis of Pingyang, Jiang Fengtang, with anticipation.","Naturally, she wanted those two dealt with as well.","They had attempted to kill her daughter several times. If they were let off lightly, wouldn’t everyone assume that she and her children were easy targets and continue bullying them in the future?","Looking at his daughter lying unconscious on the bed, Jiang Fengtang was likewise filled with fury.","He had few children—only four sons and three daughters—and treasured every one of them. Naturally, he did not want anything to happen to any of them.","This youngest daughter in particular had been frail since childhood. It had taken great effort to raise her to this age, and she had nearly lost her life at the hands of servants.","The household physician had even said that he could not be certain whether she would wake up, and had urged Jiang Fengtang to find an imperial physician to examine her.","Thinking of the adulterous pair who had caused all this, Jiang Fengtang hated them to the core.","He said coldly, “Let them off? How could that be? I’ll have their lives.”","“In a moment, I’ll have them bound and brought before Father and Mother. I’ll tell them everything and send them to the authorities for punishment.”","“They dared to murder their mistress. Not only will they pay, their families won’t escape punishment either!”","Madam Liu and Madam Zheng were naturally very pleased with the Heir’s answer.","Madam Zheng was just about to thank the Heir and the Heir’s Wife when a commotion arose in the courtyard, drawing everyone’s attention.","Madam Liu frowned. “What are the servants in the courtyard doing? Don’t they know that Fifth Girl needs quiet to recuperate? How can they be making such a racket?”","She turned to Madam Zheng. “Madam Zheng, Fifth Girl is still young, and the servants in her courtyard likely don’t obey her properly.","“When you have time, you should help her discipline those servants. Don’t let them take advantage of their young and inexperienced mistress to bully her.”","“If a maid or senior servant had been accompanying her this time, that vile pair would never have succeeded.”","Madam Zheng did not think the Heir’s Wife was using the opportunity to criticize her before the Heir or imply that she was an uncaring mother who had failed in her duty to guide her daughter. Instead, she fully agreed.","“The Madam is right. I have indeed been neglectful,” she said. “From now on, I will properly discipline the servants in Yunxi’s courtyard and guide Yunxi as well.”","Hearing the commotion outside, Jiang Fengtang’s anger also surged. He said sternly to Madam Zheng, “If anyone refuses to submit to your discipline, go to the Madam—and come to me as well.","“We will stand up for you.”","Madam Zheng hurriedly curtsied. “Then I thank the Madam and the Heir in advance.”","At that moment, someone outside began shouting loudly,","“Heir, the concubine is feeling unwell and wishes you to go see her.”","“Heir, the concubine is ill and wants Physician Wu to examine her.","“But ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​​​​‍Fifth Miss’s people have kept the household physician here and refuse to let him go. Fifth Miss and Madam Zheng clearly don’t regard the concubine at all. Please go and uphold justice for her!”","Hearing the somewhat familiar voice, everyone in the room knew who had arrived.","It was Chunlan, the senior maid serving Madam Wei.","The maids serving the Heir’s Wife had always been given names beginning with “Xia,” meaning summer. Madam Wei, wishing to outshine the Heir’s Wife, had given most of the maids around her names beginning with “Chun,” meaning spring.","Madam Liu could not help sneering. “Madam Wei is ill again?","“Of the three hundred and sixty-five days in a year, is there a single one when she isn’t sick?","“Even Fifth Girl, who was born after a difficult delivery and has always been frail, and Younger Sister Zheng, whose health was damaged, have not been ill as often as she has.”","“She merely wants to win favor through illness. After all these years, does she think no one can see through her?”","Jiang Fengtang’s face darkened.","Although that might have been true... his wife did not need to put it so bluntly.","“She simply heard that I sent someone to summon you home early and assumed something important had happened. She was afraid the benefits might fall into someone else’s hands, so she wanted to intercept you, charm you into submission, and keep the advantage for herself.”","Jiang Fengtang’s expression darkened further.","“And now she claims that there’s no household physician available because Madam Zheng and Fifth Girl are withholding him?","“She’s so well-informed—could she really not know that Fifth Girl has been unconscious for two days and still hasn’t woken up?”","“Madam Zheng has been keeping watch over Fifth Girl for two days as well. When would she have had the time to scheme against Madam Wei?”","Madam Zheng was also seething with anger. For once, she disregarded her usual restrained nature and her habit of avoiding competition with Madam Wei. She curtsied and said,","“Heir, I did not stop anyone from taking the household physician.","“I have been here with you and the Madam, questioning those two people just now. I had no idea that Younger Sister Wei had sent someone to ask for a physician.”","“Besides, there is more than one household physician in the residence. The one staying here with Fifth Girl is Physician Chen, who has always been responsible for tending to the health of the young masters and misses and specializes in pediatrics. He is not Physician Wu, whom Madam Wei usually uses.”","Jiang Fengtang suppressed his anger and said, “I know. This is not your fault.”","Even if the residence had only possessed one physician and Madam Zheng had truly withheld him, Jiang Fengtang would still have thought it was justified.","No matter how much he favored Madam Wei ordinarily, when his daughter’s life was at stake, he was not foolish enough to lose his judgment.","Chunlan continued shouting outside, completely ignoring the servants’ reprimands. Looking at his daughter lying quietly on the bed, Jiang Fengtang was overcome by an extraordinary fury.","He strode out of the room and into the courtyard, where he bellowed furiously,","“Have you no sense of propriety at all?","“You’re nothing but an ignorant servant, yet you dare run into the young miss’s courtyard and make such a scene. You’ve shown complete disrespect toward the Secondary Madam and the young miss. Is this how Madam Wei taught you?”","“My lord, the concubine is ill—”","“She’s ill every other day. Do you really think I don’t know that not a single one of those illnesses is genuine?” Jiang Fengtang cut her off.","The servant had clearly been spoiled by Madam Wei. Instead of admitting her wrongdoing when reprimanded, she actually dared to argue back.","Thinking of his own daughter, who had been harmed by two servants who knew nothing of their place, and seeing the resentment on the maid’s face, Jiang Fengtang took his anger out on her.","“Since Madam Wei doesn’t know how to teach her servants, I’ll teach her myself.”","“Someone gag her and bind her outside the courtyard. Give her thirty strokes of the cane.","“When you’re finished, throw her back to Madam Wei and have her teach her properly.","“If there’s a next time, sell her outright.”","“And punish Madam Wei by making her copy the household rules twenty times.”","...","When Madam Wei saw Chunlan being carried back like a torn rag and heard the messenger repeat the Heir’s words, her hand slipped. In a fit of rage, she accidentally knocked over the tea set, vases, and other furnishings in the room.","“Madam Zheng, Jiang Yunxi, just you wait!”"]},{"number":8,"title":"Chapter 8: We're about to starve to death, and you're still eating melon","paragraphs":["Jiang Yunxi felt as though someone had a vicious grip on her stomach, squeezing tighter and tighter with every passing moment.","Her stomach was utterly empty, and the burning ache of hunger made it impossible for her to sleep any longer. She opened her eyes.","Before her was a pale pink gauze bed curtain embroidered with trailing lotus vines, and a faint fragrance lingered in the air.","Beneath her lay a soft, cool brocade quilt, smooth and delicate to the touch.","[Host, you’re awake.]","The sudden voice in her mind reminded Jiang Yunxi of what had happened earlier.","Well then—she had transmigrated!","There was no time for sighing over her fate, much less for melancholy. Right now, Jiang Yunxi only wanted something to eat.","If she didn’t eat soon, she felt she might drop dead on the spot.","Remembering her identity after transmigrating, Jiang Yunxi knew there had to be maids keeping watch in the room. She opened her mouth, intending to call for someone.","Perhaps this body had been bedridden for too long and was still running a fever. Her throat was painfully dry. She opened and closed her mouth several times, but no sound came out.","Helpless, Jiang Yunxi—whose entire body ached—could only endure the pain and raise a hand to knock hard against the bedframe.","She thought she had used a great deal of strength, but in reality, the sound was barely audible. With the quilt muffling it further, the young maid standing several yards away with her head lowered did not hear a thing.","She knocked twice more. When no one came, she assumed there was no one in the room. Having exhausted what little strength she had, Jiang Yunxi could only give up.","[Is there anyone here? Come take care of me already!","I’m practically starving to death!]","Jiang Yunxi raged helplessly in her heart.","[Even if you want me dead, at least let me have a full meal first.","Dying from overeating is still better than dying of starvation.]","[They say that if you become a starving ghost, you won’t be able to eat your fill in your next life either. I absolutely refuse!!!]","If her awful friends ever heard that Jiang Yunxi had actually starved to death, they would laugh their heads off.","When they paid their respects to her during the Qingming Festival, they would probably burn whole roast pigs, chickens, and geese for her.","Madam Zheng had spent the night in her daughter’s quarters. After taking care of matters concerning herself and her daughter’s courtyard, she returned to continue watching over her girl.","The moment she reached the outer room of her daughter’s bedchamber, she heard her daughter’s thoughts. She immediately rushed inside, taking three steps in two.","Her daughter said she was hungry—did that mean she was awake?","As soon as Madam Zheng entered the room, she asked the young maid standing guard, “Has Miss awakened?”","“No, Madam. Miss hasn’t awakened yet,” the maid answered directly, without even checking.","Afraid that no one would attend to her again after hearing their exchange, Jiang Yunxi hurriedly replied in her heart.","[Awake! I’m awake!]","[I’ve been awake for a while now. I’m so hungry I feel like I could eat an entire cow.","But my throat hurts, and I can’t call out. I knocked on the bedframe for ages, but no one paid any attention.","I thought no one had been left here to watch over me. Turns out there was someone after all.","Is this maid deaf or blind?]","Jiang Yunxi felt utterly wronged.","In all her life, she had never experienced hunger like this.","Not even during the hungriest days of her three years in high school had she been this starving.","And now she was the daughter of a marquis’s household—a noble young lady, the child of a high-ranking official.","Was there any marquis’s daughter more miserable than her? First, the servants in the household had tried to harm her several times, and now even the maid assigned to watch over her was so inattentive.","Just what sort of person had the original owner been, that everyone thought they could bully her?","Just wait until she recovered...","Hearing her daughter’s thoughts, Madam Zheng hurried to the bedside. At once, she saw her daughter awake, her eyes darting about.","That little expression on her face—so aggrieved and pitiful.","Madam Zheng’s heart immediately ached for her. She rushed forward, gathered her daughter into her arms, and began calling her “my precious girl” and “my darling.”","At the same time, she did not forget to turn and scold the young maid.","“I told you to attend to Miss in her room. Is this how you attend to her?”","“You didn’t even notice that Miss had woken up?”","“All you do is laze around.”","Remembering what her daughter had said in her thoughts just now—that she could not call out, and had knocked on the bedframe for ages without anyone responding—","The maid had clearly been standing in the room. If she had stood a little closer, or simply glanced over from time to time, there was no way she would not have noticed that her daughter was awake.","She was plainly afraid of catching the illness and had not dared come too close.","[Host, there’s some gossip about this little maid. Want to hear it?]","Jiang Yunxi was furious. [Gossip, gossip—gossip is all you ever think about!","Can gossip fill my stomach?]","[I need food to save my life right now, not your useless gossip!]","The system instantly cowered. This host was far too unreasonable.","Who said gossip was useless? Gossip earned Gossip Points, and those could be put to great use.","Hearing her daughter once again thinking about how hungry she was, Madam Zheng no longer had the mind to reprimand the little maid. She told the maids and older servants who had followed her in,","“Drag this useless girl out. When I have time later, I’ll deal with her properly.”","When the little maid heard that Madam Zheng intended to punish her, she dropped to her knees in fright and tried to plead her case. Madam Zheng, however, cut her off sharply.","“If you dare raise your voice and disturb Miss, your punishment will be doubled.”","“Cover her mouth and drag her out.”","At once, several older maids stepped forward and hauled the little maid away.","“Suju, hurry and bring something suitable for Miss to eat.","“Miss hasn’t eaten anything for three days. She’s only had a little soup, so she must be starving by now.”","[Yes, yes—I’m practically starving to death. Hurry up and bring me food.","If you waste any more time, I’ll put on a live demonstration of ascending to heaven on the spot.]","Seeing that Miss had awakened, Suju was overjoyed.","“Please rest assured, Madam. Since we did not know when Miss would wake, it would have been too late to prepare something only after she did. Food has been kept warm in the outer room the whole time.","“I’ll bring it in right away.”","Jiang Yunxi’s eyes remained fixed on Suju’s departing back, as though she could summon the food just by staring hard enough.","Looking at the daughter in her arms, who would not spare her so much as a glance and only kept staring after Suju, Madam Zheng could not help feeling helpless.","“Look how ravenous my daughter is. She really must be starving.”","Remembering that her daughter had just said her throat was dry and she could not speak, she turned to Auntie Wu, who had just returned after seeing the little maid out.","“Auntie Wu, quickly bring some water. Make it warm. Miss has been asleep for so long—she must be thirsty.”","Before the food arrived, water would do. At least she could fill herself up with it for the moment.","After drinking two cups in a row, Jiang Yunxi still wanted more, but Madam Zheng stopped her.","“Yunxi, no more. Save some room for food.”","“Didn’t you say you were hungry?”","Just then, Suju entered with another maid carrying a tray.","The other maid caught sight of Jiang Yunxi leaning against Madam Zheng and hurried forward first, tears streaming down her face.","“Miss, you’re finally awake. You frightened this servant half to death.”","“You falling ill gave everyone quite a fright.","Madam has kept watch by your bedside for days and nights on end, and all us servants have been...”","Jiang Yunxi was on the verge of a breakdown. The food was right in front of her, yet she still could not eat it.","This woman just kept chattering on and on. Couldn’t she see that the child was staring at the dishes with eyes practically glowing green?","If she had the strength, she would have pounced on the food and snatched it for herself.","[Ah... I’m so hungry! Can you stop keeping me from eating?!]","Hearing her daughter’s near-hysterical cry, Madam Zheng’s scalp went numb.","She hurriedly cut the maid off. “Suxin, forget everything else for now. Attend to your young miss and let her eat first.","She hasn’t had a proper meal in three days. She must be starving.”","“Ah—yes...”","With tears welling in her eyes, Jiang Yunxi looked at Madam Zheng, who was holding her.","[This is my mother—my real, actual mother!","Yesterday, she saved my life from that bitch Kong, and today she’s pulled me back from the brink of starvation again and again!","From now on, she is my truest, dearest mother!]","Madam ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌‌​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​‍Zheng found it rather amusing. Was there such a thing as a fake mother?","This child had become much livelier after being ill.","That was a good thing. Before, she had seemed far too lifeless.","With the maid’s help, Madam Zheng adjusted Jiang Yunxi’s posture, letting her lean against her while the maid fed her.","In truth, Jiang Yunxi wanted to eat by herself. Being fed was far too embarrassing.","Even during chemotherapy, she had rarely received this kind of treatment.","The system’s voice sounded again. [It’s mainly because you think she feeds you too slowly to keep up with your pace.]","Jiang Yunxi replied, [No one will mistake you for a mute if you keep quiet.]","Madam Zheng: ...","“Suxin, feed her faster.”"]},{"number":9,"title":"Chapter 9: Eating Melon While Watching Shows","paragraphs":["After downing two bowls of porridge, the emptiness in her stomach finally eased, and Jiang Yunxi at last had time to complain about the food in her heart.","[Why is it all porridge? This won’t keep me full. I’ll be hungry again in no time.","I want meat. Big mouthfuls of meat.]","Having just experienced what it was like to go hungry, Jiang Yunxi didn’t want to go through it again so soon.","Madam Zheng chuckled helplessly. This child...","“Xi’er, you’ve only just woken up. You haven’t had a proper meal in three days, so for now you can only eat some porridge to ease your stomach.”","“Tomorrow—tomorrow, Mother will have someone make you chicken soup and chicken-soup noodles.”","“Once you’re better, tell me whatever you want to eat. Mother will pay the kitchen to make it for you.”","Jiang Yunxi had been sick before. How could she not know that patients shouldn’t eat anything too greasy? She was only grumbling for the sake of it.","Still, how did her mother understand her so well? Jiang Yunxi hadn’t even said anything, yet Madam Zheng had already guessed what she was thinking.","Then again, given that the original Jiang Yunxi had been born weak after a difficult delivery, Madam Zheng had probably been worrying over her since childhood. It wasn’t strange that she knew her daughter so well.","With food in her stomach, Jiang Yunxi no longer felt so anxious, and she gradually slowed down her eating.","[System, didn’t you say you had some gossip about that little maid? You can tell me now.]","She had been too hungry to listen to gossip earlier, but now she could enjoy some.","After all, gossip earned her gossip points.","Besides, she glanced at the plain porridge and tasteless side dishes. She might as well use gossip as a condiment.","The host was finally willing to listen to gossip. The System could finally earn some income.","Every time its host listened to gossip, she gained gossip points, and the System could skim a little off the top as well.","That wily System had tricked it several times, leaving it deeply in debt.","On top of that, with this host’s cunning personality, she would probably find more ways to swindle it in the future.","It had to get this sly host to listen to more gossip, pay off its debt, and save up a little more. Otherwise, it would end up in debt again later.","[Host, that little maid was placed in your courtyard by your half-sister.]","Madam Zheng frowned. That little maid was Jiang Yunshu’s person?","No wonder she had been so careless in serving her daughter.","She had stayed in the room to keep watch, yet hadn’t even realized that her daughter had woken up.","Jiang Yunshu had arranged for her to stay by her daughter’s side. She certainly couldn’t have had good intentions. Madam Zheng might as well take this opportunity to drive the girl out.","Jiang Yunxi, who still hadn’t fully adjusted to her current identity, instinctively reacted when she heard that the maid had been sent by her half-sister.","[My half-sister? Who’s that?]","Madam ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌‌​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​‍Zheng’s heart jolted.","“My heavens! My daughter has had a high fever for so long. She couldn’t have been burned stupid, could she?","‘My half-sister’? Who else would you mean? You only have one half-sister.","You make it sound as though you have several.”","Just as Madam Zheng was wondering whether she should ask her daughter a few questions to confirm that the fever hadn’t damaged her mind and turned her into a fool, Jiang Yunxi’s next thought immediately put her at ease.","[Oh, you mean Jiang Yunshu.","She’s the one who arranged for that maid to come?","What did she put her in my courtyard for?]","[What else? To spy on you, of course.","But that maid wasn’t originally placed there by Jiang Yunshu. Jiang Yunshu bought her off later.]","[That maid knew she had someone backing her, and she also thought Bibi was a sickly weakling. So whenever... she didn’t care much about serving Bibi.","Several times when Bibi fell ill, that maid was on night watch but didn’t pay attention. Bibi kicked off her quilt, and the maid, busy sleeping soundly herself, didn’t even bother to cover her.","Everyone knew Bibi was frail, but no one suspected her. That only made her grow even more careless in her duties.]","At some point, Madam Zheng had tightened her grip around Jiang Yunxi’s arm.","The pain made Jiang Yunxi swallow the porridge that had just been stuffed into her mouth in a hurry.","“Mother, please don’t squeeze so hard. You’re hurting me.”","“Ah—oh.” Madam Zheng came back to herself and quickly let go.","Worried that she might accidentally hurt her daughter again, she stopped holding Jiang Yunxi’s arm and instead clutched the quilt covering her.","Madam Zheng was seething. That little maid could not be let off lightly. She would have someone interrogate her thoroughly later.","And Jiang Yunshu could not be let off either.","She needed to take advantage of the Heir’s current guilt toward her daughter and report the matter to him, so that he would punish Jiang Yunshu properly.","Otherwise, once the Heir was bewitched by Madam Wei, and that mother and daughter coaxed him around, the matter might be brushed aside yet again.","But when her daughter and the System talked about her, why did they keep calling her “old Bibi” and “Bibi”? If Madam Zheng hadn’t known who they were talking about, she would have been completely baffled.","[By the way, she followed us to the rear garden this time.","She was supposed to hide, and that maid was supposed to find her. But the maid was being lazy and went off to play with someone else. That’s why Bibi wasn’t found until much later, delaying her treatment.]","Jiang Yunxi thought, [Holy crap. So she was an accomplice.","And she’s harmed Bibi more than once!]","[That’s right.]","[She’s Bibi’s maid. What good would come to her if Bibi died?","If she didn’t want to serve Bibi, she could have said so clearly and left.]","[How could she not want to serve Bibi? Bibi had a gentle nature and a mild temper. She rarely punished the servants, so compared with the other young masters and misses in the household, she was much easier to serve.","Her mistress was easy to handle, and every time she made her mistress ill, she could run to Jiang Yunshu to claim credit and receive a generous reward. It was practically the perfect arrangement.]","[Holy crap. So she treated Bibi as a way to make money, deliberately making her sick so she could profit from it.]","The System said, [Bingo. Exactly.]","Jiang Yunxi felt her fists clench. That little maid was utterly inhuman.","And Jiang Yunshu was no better. How could anyone be so cruel to her own younger sister?","She had known that the ancient inner households were full of unrest, but most conflicts were between legitimate and illegitimate daughters. She hadn’t expected there to be such viciousness even between half-sisters...","After sorting through the original owner’s memories, Jiang Yunxi couldn’t help frowning.","[System, Jiang Yunshu is fifteen by nominal age, while Bibi is nine. There’s a six-year difference between them.","Bibi couldn’t possibly be a threat to her, so why can’t she tolerate Bibi?]","[Bibi was already frail, and Jiang Yunshu had people make her sick time and again. She’s clearly trying to take Bibi’s life.","Could Bibi have offended her somehow?]","The System said, [I don’t know.]","Jiang Yunxi inhaled sharply.","[You don’t know? Aren’t you the omniscient Gossip System, the all-knowing Gossip System? How can you not even know this?","You knew that Nanny Kong’s lover was Steward Ma. How can you not know why Jiang Yunshu wants to harm me?]","The System replied righteously, [Host, I’m only a beginner-level system. My functions aren’t powerful enough yet.","I can only learn someone’s gossip after meeting that person. I can’t extend my investigations to other people.]","[By listening to the little maid’s gossip, I could find out that Jiang Yunshu instructed her to harm you, but I can’t learn Jiang Yunshu’s motive.]","Jiang Yunxi: Useless System.","Still, the System was somewhat useful. At the very least, it had revealed the enemy hiding in the shadows.","She just couldn’t offend Jiang Yunshu too badly for now.","[Then what do you need in order to find out?]","[You have to see her in person once. Once I’ve seen her, I’ll be able to listen to her gossip in the future and find out why she hates you.]","Seeing her once shouldn’t be difficult. They were sisters from the same household, after all. There would surely be opportunities to meet.","[Oh, and that little maid had grown very bold after getting away with harming you several times without being discovered.","The silver and jewelry Jiang Yunshu rewarded her with are all hidden in a chest in her room.]","[Jiang Yunshu is bold too. She actually gave away jewelry she didn’t even like. Those are all clear-cut pieces of evidence.]","Madam Zheng lowered her eyes. Perfect, that saved her the trouble of hunting for evidence herself.","Jiang Yunxi: This is great. Once I recover from this illness, I'll frame that little maid with some petty mistake, search her belongings, and expose the whole mess.","[Ding! Host has successfully eaten the drama of the backstabbing little maid. Gossip points +100.]","Jiang Yunxi was over the moon. Another 100 points added to her tally.","The Gossip-Eating System was the best by far, way better than those quest systems or romance conquest systems.","But she couldn't let the System know that, or it would get too complacent.","[System, from now on, every time I successfully eat a piece of gossip, report my total current gossip points, okay? That way I don't have to go check the count myself.]","[Understood, Host. Happy to assist.","Host's current total gossip points: 700.]","System, I'm so happy. I finally got some points coming in today, I'm one step closer to paying off all my debts.","Keep pushing forward.","[Host, there is a piece of gossip related to your biological mother. Would you like to eat it?]"]},{"number":10,"title":"Chapter 10: Someone Wants to Harm Your Mother","paragraphs":["Hearing the system in her daughter’s mind say, 【Host, there’s some juicy gossip about your birth mother. Want to hear it?】 Madam Zheng was struck numb.","After hearing her daughter’s inner thoughts several times, and after what had happened with Nanny Kong, Madam Zheng had come to completely trust the system’s abilities.","It could definitely dig up every one of her secrets.","Although she had never committed any crimes or done anything wrong, she still had private matters she did not want anyone to know about.","And she certainly did not want her daughter to know.","That would be far too embarrassing.","Madam Zheng opened her mouth, wanting to stop it, but she had clearly forgotten what had happened the day before.","She tried to speak, only to discover that no sound came out.","Madam Zheng was even more dumbfounded. She could not even stop the system. What was she supposed to do?","Perhaps she should leave immediately. Hadn’t the system just said that as long as it had never met someone, it could not expose their gossip?","But they had already met. Even if she left, the system could still expose it.","What was she going to do?","While Madam Zheng was fretting, Jiang Yunxi was struggling with the same dilemma.","Should she hear the gossip about her own mother or not?","If she did, it seemed somewhat inappropriate.","If she learned that her mother had done something bad, how was she supposed to treat her afterward?","Her mother seemed to have treated the original owner quite well. She had stayed by her daughter’s side while she was ill. She was clearly a good mother.","If Jiang Yunxi found out that she had done something wrong, could she really bring herself to do anything to her?","But if her mother had truly committed some unforgivable evil, the education Jiang Yunxi had received would make it impossible for her to pretend she knew nothing.","Rather than being put in a difficult position later, it would be better to...","【System, I don’t want to hear it.】","System: Other than when she had been desperately hungry just now, the host had never refused gossip before. Why was she refusing this time?","【Host, gossip about yourself or your relatives earns more gossip points than gossip about outsiders.】 The system tried to tempt her.","Jiang Yunxi was resolute. 【I’m not listening.】","【Host, it’s fine. Just listen. Your mother won’t know that you’ve learned her secret.】","Madam Zheng: I know. I heard everything.","Daughter, whatever you do, don’t listen.","Perhaps because she was overly agitated, Madam Zheng shifted a few times. This startled Jiang Yunxi, who was in her arms, and drew the girl’s attention away from the system.","Earlier, Jiang Yunxi had been so hungry that although she had noticed Madam Zheng, she had not had the time to think about anything else.","Now that she was full and satisfied, she finally had time to look properly.","The moment she turned her head and saw Madam Zheng, Jiang Yunxi froze in stunned amazement. Her heart began to pound wildly.","【Oh my heavens, my mother is gorgeous!】","Madam Zheng could not help but blush faintly.","What was wrong with this child? Why was she acting as if she had never seen her mother before?","Could the fever really have damaged her brain?","Madam Zheng could not help worrying again that her daughter had been turned into a fool.","Madam Zheng was wearing a lake-blue, brightly embroidered brocade dress, with elegant orchids embroidered along the hem.","Her long, black hair, dark as a waterfall, was simply gathered into a bun and adorned with two plain hairpins.","Though her attire was simple, everything was perfectly balanced, giving her a dignified and refined air.","【Holy crap, my mother is beautiful!","Forgive my lack of education. I’ve racked my brains, but I can’t think of any other words to describe her. All I know is that she’s beautiful.","Beautiful is enough.】","【With my mother’s bearing and presence, anyone who didn’t know better would think she was a young lady from an aristocratic family.","She’s practically a fairy descended to earth.】","【With her poise, anyone who didn’t know better would think she was the lady of the house from some prominent family.】","System: 【Your mother really is a young lady from an aristocratic family. With that kind of bearing and presence, there’s nothing strange about it.","She was raised from childhood to be the lady of the household.】","Jiang Yunxi frowned. 【Then how did she end up as a concubine?】","Madam Zheng’s eyes darkened.","Was her daughter blaming her? Blaming her for becoming someone else’s concubine and making her a child of secondary birth as well?","【That’s because...】","Jiang Yunxi suddenly realized what was happening. 【System, shut up. I don’t want to hear it.","You’re definitely trying to use this opportunity to make me listen to gossip about my own mother.】","【I’m telling you, whether my mother is a principal wife or a concubine, she’s still my mother.","I believe she must have had her reasons for becoming a concubine.】","【So what if she’s a concubine? My mother is so beautiful that even as a concubine, she’s the most beautiful one.","She’s a concubine who looks just like a principal wife.","Haven’t you noticed that all these maids and nannies address her as Madam? They obviously acknowledge in their hearts that she’s no different from the principal wife.】","Madam Zheng’s slightly downcast mood instantly brightened like the sky after a shower, and she was delighted.","At the same time, she found herself both amused and exasperated. How could this child praise her mother like that?","And ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌​​​​‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌‍what did she mean by “a concubine who looks just like a principal wife”? That was not something one could say casually. A concubine was a concubine. Even if she was treated as a secondary wife, she was still a concubine.","It seemed she would have to teach her daughter properly in the future and stop her from saying such careless things, lest she attract people’s hatred.","The Heir’s Wife had already treated the three of them—mother and children—quite well.","That was partly because Madam Zheng had always shown the principal wife the utmost respect and acted with great caution, while also making sure that her two children understood their status and never competed with the legitimate children.","But the principal wife truly was fairly broad-minded.","The system was furious. What was wrong with this host? It was speaking perfectly clearly. Why couldn’t she understand?","Had it ever said that her mother was unattractive? Had it ever said that she should not have become a concubine?","It already knew why she had become one. It knew she had her own difficulties. How could it possibly blame her?","【Host, can you stop taking my words out of context?","Did this system ever say that your mother isn’t beautiful? Did I ever say she shouldn’t have become a concubine?】","【I’m telling you to listen to the gossip about your mother for a reason.","It’s for your sake, and for your mother’s.】","As she listened to the system’s voice growing even louder than her own, Jiang Yunxi inexplicably felt like backing down.","But even if she lost, she could not lose face. She absolutely could not let the system get the upper hand.","If she allowed it to climb all over her, wouldn’t she be unable to stand up to it in the future?","From beginning to end, she had to make sure the system understood who was the host and who was merely the system.","Jiang Yunxi planted her hands on her hips like a tiny tyrant and raised her voice even louder, determined to overpower the system.","【Then tell me how exactly you’re helping me and my mother.】","Madam Zheng’s ears were filled with the sound of the host and system arguing. Their voices were so loud that her head began to buzz.","Her daughter was still a child, and whatever this system was, it acted like an immature child too. It could actually get into an argument with a child.","The system grew angrier and raised its voice again.","【Your mother suffered difficult deliveries both times she gave birth. When she gave birth to you, she nearly died along with the baby.","Before she became pregnant with you, she even miscarried once. Do you really think all of that was accidental?】","Jiang Yunxi fell silent.","Madam Zheng’s heart jolted as well. From the system’s words, it seemed that none of those incidents had been accidents.","Jiang Yunxi unconsciously lowered her voice. 【So none of it was accidental? Someone was trying to harm my mother?】","Seeing that the host had lowered her voice, the system felt that it had finally gained the upper hand. It felt as if it were about to ascend to a higher plane of existence.","Perhaps it should no longer be content with remaining a basic system. After exposing gossip several times, it was probably time for it to level up.","【Naturally.","How could there be so many accidents, all of them happening to your mother?】","【Your mother is still being poisoned from time to time!】","The system threw out yet another bombshell. Madam Zheng clenched her fists, while Jiang Yunxi’s eyes widened in fury.","Excellent. Her forty-meter broadsword was already impatient to taste blood.","Niohuru Jiang Yunxi was about to make her dazzling entrance.","【Who exactly is trying to harm my mother?","I’ll find that person and hack them into pieces!】","Memories steeped in countless novels came rushing back.","【System, hurry up and tell me—is it Madam? In other words, my nominal stepmother?】"]},{"number":11,"title":"Chapter 11: It's Too Hard to Support a Family","paragraphs":["“System, tell me quickly. Was it my nominal stepmother who harmed my mother?”","Hearing her daughter ask the System that question, Madam Zheng’s heart tightened.","“I don’t know.”","Hearing that answer, Jiang Yunxi flopped backward in frustration. Madam Zheng, who was holding her, was caught off guard and fell backward with her.","Madam Zheng’s head struck the bedframe with a loud thump.","Jiang Yunxi was no better. Her head slammed into Madam Zheng’s chest, causing a second injury.","Once she realized the position they were in, Jiang Yunxi regretted it terribly.","She shouldn’t have assumed she was still on her six-foot bed, with pillows behind her and free to fall backward however she pleased.","See? She’d hurt someone again.","Her whole body was sore, and she didn’t have the strength to climb up on her own, so she could only call out, “Mother, are you all right?”","“Mother, I’m sorry. It’s all my fault. I forgot for a moment that—”","Seeing how guilt-ridden her daughter was, Madam Zheng had no time to worry about the pain in her head and chest. She quickly comforted her. “Don’t worry, Yunxi. Mother is fine.”","The maids and nanny beside them immediately came forward. They first helped Jiang Yunxi up, then helped Madam Zheng settle herself.","One nimble-handed maid hurriedly rubbed the back of Madam Zheng’s head and massaged her chest.","They had finished eating, and Madam Zheng was worried that Jiang Yunxi might get emotional again and hurt someone else. Jiang Yunxi spoke up.","“Help me lie down. Don’t carry me anymore.”","“My whole body hurts. I’ll be more comfortable lying down.”","Hearing Jiang Yunxi’s thoughts, Madam Zheng no longer insisted on holding her. She quickly ordered, “Help Miss lie down.”","“Go see whether the medicine is ready, and whether the household physician has arrived.”","“Is it bitter Chinese medicine? I refuse to drink it.”","“I have medicine from the System. It’s much more effective than Chinese medicine, and I don’t have to suffer through the bitterness.”","“If I hadn’t taken two doses of medicine from the System, I probably wouldn’t have woken up yet.”","Madam Zheng couldn’t help coughing once. They still had to prepare the medicine, or outsiders might become suspicious.","At worst, she would send everyone away when her daughter drank it and find an excuse to leave as well.","The household physician still had to examine her daughter. Otherwise, there would be no explanation for her sudden recovery.","After complaining, Jiang Yunxi continued pressing the System about the question from earlier.","“System, how can you not know whether my nominal stepmother was the one who harmed my mother?”","The System sighed. “Host, did you forget what I told you earlier?”","“By learning your mother’s secrets, I discovered that someone was trying to harm her. I also found out that the midwife who harmed her was connected to a concubine in the household surnamed Wei.”","“As for anything else, I can’t tell just by learning your mother’s secrets.”","“I’ll know once I see your stepmother in person.”","Before Jiang Yunxi could ask again, the System hurriedly added, “And don’t ask whether that concubine surnamed Wei is the real mastermind. I can’t tell just by learning your mother’s secrets.”","“I’ll have to learn Concubine Wei’s secrets to know.”","“If you want to uncover the truth, you’d better recover quickly and take me to meet your stepmother and Concubine Wei.”","“Oh, and your half-sister too.”","Madam Zheng closed her eyes, hiding the emotions in them.","Madam Wei. Very well.","You harmed me, and your daughter harmed mine. From now on, we are enemies.","Madam Wei might be favored, but she did not manage the household. The midwife she used had been hired by the Heir’s Wife. Even if the midwife had entered the residence a few days early, could Madam Wei really have conspired with her in just those few days?","Did Madam Wei even have that kind of brains?","But if the Heir’s Wife was behind it, the System should have known. It even knew about Nanny Kong and Steward Ma.","Madam Zheng felt a headache coming on.","“Forget it. There’s no point thinking about it when I can’t figure anything out.”","“I’ll wait until my daughter meets...”","Jiang Yunxi sorted through the System’s words and finally clarified a few things.","“Both of the difficult births and the miscarriage were connected to Concubine Wei?”","The System nodded, then remembered that it had no physical form and Jiang Yunxi couldn’t see it nod. It quickly answered aloud, “The midwives involved in both births deliberately caused trouble and delayed the deliveries.”","“As for the miscarriage, it happened because your mother took medicine with cooling properties.”","“The medicine was administered by a maid whom Madam Wei had planted beside her.”","“Oh, right. That maid has since become a nanny. She served your mother for a long time and is still working in your mother’s courtyard.”","“She even continues to sneak things your mother shouldn’t be eating into her meals.”","“Who is it?”","The System gave her a name, but Jiang Yunxi had no idea who that was.","Jiang Yunxi didn’t recognize the name, but Madam Zheng did. In her heart, she immediately sentenced that woman.","Now that she understood the System’s limitations, Jiang Yunxi stopped asking questions and could only say, “Next time I find a chance to go to my mother’s courtyard, I’ll figure out a way to meet her.”","“Then you can learn her secrets and expose everything she’s done.”","“Find all the evidence proving that she colluded with Madam Wei.”","“All right, Host.”","Madam Zheng lowered her eyes. It seemed she would have to keep that woman around a little longer, so that her daughter could...","This System of her daughter’s was far more useful than having someone else interrogate the woman.","People said that those who survived a great disaster would have good fortune afterward. Looking at her daughter, Madam Zheng could see that it was true.","“Host, although your mother’s health is somewhat better than yours, it still isn’t very good.”","“If she doesn’t take proper care of herself, I’m afraid she won’t live much longer.”","Madam Zheng smiled inwardly. She had known this for a long time.","When she gave birth to her daughter, she had barely survived. Being able to accompany her daughter as she grew up was already a blessing beyond measure.","If Heaven could give her a few more years—enough to see her daughter marry and have children—that would be even better.","But would Heaven grant her such a wish...?","Jiang Yunxi’s heart tightened. She couldn’t help looking toward Madam Zheng, only to meet her mother’s gaze.","Feeling the love that could not be concealed in those eyes, Jiang Yunxi grew embarrassed and turned her face away.","In her modern life, her biological parents had both been reserved people who were not good at expressing their feelings. She had never been looked at like this before.","It left her at a loss.","“System, you said that one Body-Strengthening Pill could cure my frail constitution. What about my mother?”","“Host, don’t worry. One Body-Strengthening Pill can cure her as well.”","“So you need to hurry up and learn more secrets. Then you can earn more gossip points and exchange them for the pills.”","“You and your mother need one pill each, which means you’ll need 1,000 points.”","“Like you, your mother has taken medicine for many years and has also been deliberately poisoned. A Pill of Immunity to All Poisons is necessary too.”","“You know the price of that pill. The lifelong version costs 1,500 points. Altogether, that makes 2,500.”","“Oh, and you also have a full brother.”","“His birth was quite difficult too, so his health is probably...”","“You and your mother have both been deliberately targeted. It’s hard to say whether your brother has escaped the same fate.”","In order to make its host stronger and encourage her to uncover more secrets, the System was working itself to the bone. After all, the more secrets she uncovered, the more kickbacks it could earn.","After doing the math, Jiang Yunxi felt as though dark clouds had gathered over her head. The total for her and her mother was already 2,500 points. Add the 2,000 points needed for her brother, and that made 4,500.","She could choose not to care about that brother, but Jiang Yunxi knew that in ancient times, where sons were valued over daughters, life would be extremely difficult without a full brother to support her—whether in her own family or in her future husband’s household.","Although she also had an older legitimate brother and two half-brothers, she had not grown particularly close to any of them, having spent most of her life secluded in the inner chambers.","Besides, ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌​​​​‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌‍in the original host’s memories, her own brother had always treated her well. Jiang Yunxi couldn’t possibly abandon him.","Before she had even gotten started, she was already saddled with 4,500 in debt. Jiang Yunxi felt the pressure mounting.","【System, is there any quick way to earn Gossip Points?","The pressure of supporting a family is just too much.","I only have 700 right now, and I’m still a long way from 4,500.","I’m afraid the requirements will only get higher from here.】","【Yes. Consume more gossip.】","【Once I level up, the range of gossip you can consume will expand, and the Gossip Points will come pouring in.】","Forced beneath the burden of supporting her family, Jiang Yunxi gritted her teeth.","【Eat, eat, eat! I’ll consume gossip like my life depends on it.】","【From today onward, the moment I open my eyes, I’m going to hunt for gossip.","From now on, just call me the Little Gossip Expert.】","【Host, you’ve been consuming your mother’s gossip all this time. Why not finish it?","If you don’t finish it, you won’t get any Gossip Points, will you?】"]},{"number":12,"title":"Chapter 12: Your Mother Once Had Someone She Admired","paragraphs":["When the System asked whether she wanted to finish eating her birth mother’s gossip, Jiang Yunxi gritted her teeth. 【Eat it!】","She had already eaten this much of her mother’s gossip. She might as well get it all over with in one go.","Judging from what she had learned so far, her mother didn’t seem to have done anything shameful. If anything, she was the victim—the biggest innocent fool of them all.","Since that was the case, there was nothing to worry about.","Even if her mother had done something wrong, only she and the System would know about it. They could simply pretend they didn’t.","Who knew? Perhaps if she dug deeply enough, she might even find the culprit who had harmed her mother.","Madam Zheng wanted to stop her, but judging from what had happened just now, there was no way she could.","Still, simply standing there and listening to her daughter eat her own gossip was rather embarrassing.","“Forget it. If I can’t afford to provoke it, I can at least hide from it.”","Although she wanted to know what kind of gossip the System was about to reveal—and whether it would expose more details she didn’t know—Madam Zheng truly couldn’t bear to stay any longer.","“Forget it. I’ll go outside and listen.","“Judging from what happened yesterday, I should still be able to hear everything even if I’m outside...”","In any case, she could hear her daughter’s thoughts from outside the room, and without having to face her directly, it wouldn’t be quite so embarrassing.","“Yunxi, get some rest. Mother is going to deal with that little maid from earlier.”","When Jiang Yunxi heard that she intended to deal with the maid, she wanted to stop her. Her mother probably didn’t yet know that the girl had been planted by Jiang Yunshu. If they dismissed her without investigating, wouldn’t that be letting Jiang Yunshu off too easily?","Madam Zheng seemed to understand what she was thinking and spoke before she could say anything.","“She was so careless in her duties. I’m going to question her carefully and find out what she was really thinking—and who sent her.”","At that, Jiang Yunxi’s hand, which had been reaching out like Erkang’s, slowly withdrew.","【I wonder if it’s true that mothers and daughters are connected by heart. My mother can actually guess what I’m thinking.","【First she knew I was hungry, and now she knows I want to investigate whether someone ordered that little maid to do this.】","Madam Zheng felt deeply awkward inside. If it weren’t for... how could she possibly have guessed?","Unable to explain herself, Madam Zheng hurried out, taking several people with her.","Jiang Yunxi closed her eyes and pretended to sleep while focusing on the gossip.","【Your mother’s maiden name is Zheng Qingzhi. She comes from the prestigious Zheng family, a respected scholarly clan. Your maternal grandfather was once the head of Qinglan Academy.","【Qinglan Academy was founded by the Zheng family and has been around for more than a hundred years.】","【Wow...】 Jiang Yunxi couldn’t help exclaiming. 【A school with a tradition spanning more than a century was founded by the Zheng family. No wonder they’re considered a prestigious scholarly clan.】","Jiang Yunxi knew that academies in this era were nothing like modern schools, and Qinglan Academy had been established for more than a hundred years.","Many officials in the imperial court had probably studied there.","Jiang Yunxi frowned, unable to suppress her doubts.","【A woman from a prestigious scholarly family, the daughter of an academy headmaster—someone who values her reputation above all else. She’d probably rather marry a poor scholar than become the concubine of a son from another aristocratic family.","【So how did my mother end up...?】","Hearing her daughter’s doubts, Madam Zheng, who was listening to her thoughts outside while ordering people to search the little maid’s room, couldn’t help sighing inwardly as memories of the past surfaced.","The System truly had a storyteller’s instincts. It deliberately let out a sigh before saying:","【This goes back to the previous struggle for the throne.】","【To put it simply, your maternal grandfather refused to support any particular prince. He didn’t want the academy to become a breeding ground for one prince’s faction. That prince considered him stubborn and disobedient, so he decided to eliminate him.","【After a series of fabrications and framed charges, your maternal grandfather was convicted.","【He had been wrongfully accused, his reputation and a scholar’s integrity stained beyond repair. In the end, he died to prove his innocence.","【He died and escaped all his troubles, but that left his wife, children, and the rest of the family behind...】","Jiang Yunxi knitted her brows tightly. 【My maternal grandfather was framed. Didn’t anyone else do anything?】","【That man was a powerful contender for the throne. Even if people knew your maternal grandfather had been wronged, what could they do?","【And so your mother went from being a young lady of a prestigious scholarly family—the daughter of an academy headmaster—to the daughter of a disgraced criminal.】","【You also have an older maternal uncle and a younger maternal aunt. Your uncle is the eldest, while your aunt is the youngest.","【Once the family’s reputation was ruined, your mother happened to be at the age when marriage proposals came calling. Naturally, arranging her marriage became a difficult matter.】","【That was when the wife of the Marquis of Pingyang’s heir came to the family and proposed a match on behalf of the Heir to the Marquis of Pingyang—in other words, your father. She wanted your mother to become his secondary wife.","【Your father had once been your maternal grandfather’s student. At the time, he asked his wife to make the proposal for two reasons. First, he was worried about his teacher’s family and wanted to protect them under the Marquis of Pingyang’s household, deterring anyone who might try to take advantage of them.】","【I have to say, your father handled that part quite well. He was much better than those ungrateful, heartless wretches.","【At the very least, he was willing to provide help when your family was at its most desperate. Of course, the fact that he made your mother his concubine is open to criticism—but what else could he have done? He was already married and even had children.】","【He had continuously supported your maternal grandmother, your uncle, and your aunt, paying for their education and daily expenses and allowing them to live with servants attending to them.","【You have to understand that, at the time, that prince was still a powerful contender for the throne.","【Later, once the struggle for succession had settled and that prince had lost, your father joined forces with other officials who had studied at Qinglan Academy to overturn the case against your maternal grandfather. They restored his good name and returned the family property that had been confiscated.","【Judging from all this, your father really was beyond reproach.】","【Host, you should know that some of the people who harmed your maternal grandfather had also come from Qinglan Academy.","【Compared with them, this System has to give your father a huge thumbs-up.】","Outside the room, Madam Zheng couldn’t help smiling faintly. Although the Heir had been rather questionable in his treatment of Madam Wei, he truly had an impeccable character.","If he hadn’t shown her family such great kindness, she would never have willingly become his concubine and spent all these years keeping a low profile and enduring everything in his household.","Hearing the System praise him, Jiang Yunxi grew somewhat curious about her cheap father, whom she had never even met.","【Actually, it was the Heir’s Wife who suggested making your mother a concubine.","【Madam Wei is your father’s maternal cousin. She ran wild in the inner household and didn’t even show the Heir’s Wife any respect.","【The Heir’s Wife thought that your mother was your father’s junior schoolmate and that, now that her family had fallen into trouble, your father had always remained concerned about her. She assumed he had feelings for your mother, so she arranged the match on his behalf, hoping to use your mother to suppress Madam Wei.】","Jiang ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌‌​​‌​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​‍Yunxi couldn’t help rolling her eyes.","How had she ended up in ancient times?","A woman arranging for her own husband to take a concubine—in other words, finding him a mistress. In modern society, that would be an utterly outrageous, world-shattering thing.","Yet in ancient times, it had become something expected of the lady of the household.","If, after she grew up, her future husband asked her to arrange a concubine for him, Jiang Yunxi felt she might consider arranging for him to become a widower instead.","Given her current status as a daughter of the Marquis’s household, even if she was only a secondary daughter, she should still receive a respectable dowry when she married.","Her husband’s family probably wouldn’t be of low status either, so she likely wouldn’t have to worry about money.","Women in ancient times didn’t need to work for a living.","As for managing household affairs, she was a secondary daughter. She probably wouldn’t become the principal wife of a clan heir or the lady of the house.","At most, she would become the wife of a secondary son or the youngest son of the principal wife. She wouldn’t have to manage the household.","That meant she could have both money and free time.","She would first find a way to move out and live separately, then arrange for herself to become a widow.","Money, free time, no need to serve her parents-in-law, no need to manage the household, and no pressure to bear children.","Damn, it was practically her dream life as a wealthy widow.","Of course, it would be even better if she could have a child or two before becoming widowed.","While Jiang Yunxi was lost in her fantasies, the System continued rambling on.","[But who would have thought that after your mother entered the household, she was so grateful for your father’s kindness to her family that she didn’t want to cause him any trouble. She always chose to keep the peace, treating those above her with deference and those below her with kindness. She never competed with Madam Wei for status.]","[That left the Heir’s Wife completely unprepared.]","Jiang Yunxi observed a moment of silence for her stepmother. She had thought that by supporting one woman to suppress the other and provoking them into fighting, the Heir’s Wife could sit back and reap the benefits.","Who could have expected that the two of them wouldn’t fight at all? Instead, another formidable rival had appeared.","Fortunately, her mother wasn’t one to stir up trouble. Otherwise, the Heir’s Wife would probably have had a massive headache.","[Still, your mother’s arrival wasn’t entirely without effect.","With your mother there as a comparison, Madam Wei really doesn’t dare act as arrogantly as she used to.","She’s your father’s cousin, while your mother is your father’s junior fellow disciple. They’re both “younger sisters”—so who’s afraid of whom?]","Madam Zheng frowned. What was that last sentence supposed to mean?","[Your mother was sabotaged twice during difficult labors and even suffered a miscarriage once. I’ve already mentioned that before, so I won’t go into it again.]","[Host,] the system said excitedly, [let me tell you something. Before your mother was married, she had someone she was in love with.]"]},{"number":13,"title":"Chapter 13: The Extraordinary Uncles and Aunts","paragraphs":["When the System said, “Host, before your mother was married, she had someone she was fond of,” Madam Zheng panicked.","How did this System know everything?","What admirer? Even she herself didn’t know about that. How could it?","And Yunxi was still just a child. How could it say such things in front of her without the slightest regard?","Madam Zheng had no idea that the soul inhabiting her daughter’s body was that of someone in her twenties—only a few years younger than herself.","It was one thing for her daughter to know about other matters. It was even fine for her to learn about the dangers of human nature. But this matter... absolutely could not be allowed to reach her ears.","But how was she supposed to stop it?","Just then, a servant entered to report, “Madam, Physician Chen heard that Miss has woken up and would like to come examine her.”","Madam Zheng was overjoyed. “Quick, quick, invite him in.”","With Physician Chen making a fuss nearby, her daughter surely wouldn’t keep gossiping about her with that System.","Madam Zheng entered her daughter’s bedchamber first and instructed her softly, “Yunxi, don’t go to sleep yet. Wait until the physician has examined you.”","“The medicine will be ready soon too. Take it before you sleep.”","And stop chatting with the System about my gossip. You’ve taken all those other medicines, so you’d better pray that the physician doesn’t notice anything unusual.","At that moment, the brainwaves of Jiang Yunxi and Madam Zheng miraculously synchronized.","【Damn, System, I woke up this quickly because of you, not that physician. But no one can know about your existence—or those medicines. If he takes the credit, won’t he be getting credit for something he didn’t do?】","The System nodded firmly. 【Naturally.】","Jiang Yunxi frowned. 【Wouldn’t that be setting him up?","What if he starts thinking he’s an amazing doctor? Next time something like this happens, he might treat someone without knowing his own limits and end up making them worse. Wouldn’t that be harming people?】","【He isn’t stupid. He should know how capable he is and probably won’t claim all the credit.】","【Hard to say. What if he...】","While helping her daughter tidy herself up, Madam Zheng said casually,","【Physician Chen does have some skill. Over the years, the young masters and misses in the household have all benefited from his care.","Your health has also been nurtured and maintained thanks in large part to him.","He’s a very modest man.】","What Madam Zheng meant was: Yunxi, stop worrying about this.","【A very modest man?】 Jiang Yunxi’s mind relaxed a little. 【Then he probably won’t claim this as his own achievement. Maybe he’ll blame it on luck—or my good fortune.","In any case, he’s taken care of my health for so many years. Even if he hasn’t earned the credit, he’s put in the work. Letting him take a little advantage won’t hurt.】","Remembering her daughter’s earlier inner thoughts, Madam Zheng suspected that Yunxi seemed rather short of those gossip points.","Her eyes shifted, and she smoothly changed the subject.","“Physician Chen has rendered great service by waking you this time. The Marchioness will certainly reward him, and your father will too once he returns from the office.","“I’ll have to give him a good reward myself later.”","Jiang Yunxi’s eyes widened. 【The physician already receives a monthly salary.","If he cures me, he’ll get three extra rewards on top of that!】","“Once Physician Chen has checked your pulse and confirmed that your condition has improved, I’ll also send someone to inform your grandfather and grandmother.","“You’ve been unconscious for several days, and they were terribly worried. We must let them know as soon as possible so they can set their minds at ease.”","“When they learn that Physician Chen cured you, they’ll surely reward him too.”","Jiang Yunxi began counting on her fingers.","Three plus two equals five.","So, after she recovered, Physician Chen would receive five rewards.","Her mother didn’t count, since she had no idea how much money Madam Zheng possessed. But the other two couples were the Marquis and the Marchioness, and the heir and the Heir’s Wife. Their wealth went without saying.","Their rewards would definitely be lavish.","【Physician Chen is going to make a killing this time.","And curing me wasn’t even his doing.】","Exactly!","Yunxi, weren’t you worried about how to earn those so-called gossip points? Physician Chen is taking advantage of you, so just dig up some gossip about him and claw back a little of what he’s getting.","Stop targeting your poor mother.","Thinking of those five rewards, Jiang Yunxi felt as though she could see piles of little coins flying away from her.","If only all that money could be given to her.","Part miser and part cheapskate, Jiang Yunxi grew furious.","【System, dig into him. When Physician Chen arrives, investigate him thoroughly.","Ideally, find out everything—even whether he wet the bed as a child.】","【He’s getting so many benefits from me. I have to find a way to make up the difference!】","Since the host had taken the initiative to start gossiping without needing any prompting, how could the System refuse?","【Don’t worry, Host. I’ll investigate him thoroughly later. I won’t even spare the space between his toes.】","That wording sounded oddly unpleasant. Jiang Yunxi looked disgusted.","【Forget the spaces between his toes. Just strip his secrets bare.】","【Don’t worry, Host. Leave it to me.】","Remembering that she had already finished eating up her mother’s gossip but still hadn’t received any gossip points, Jiang Yunxi reminded the System,","【System, I’ve finished with my mother’s gossip. Shouldn’t you give me my reward now?】","The System was bewildered. 【Finished? No, you haven’t. I haven’t even told you about your mother’s admirer from before she was married.】","Madam Zheng was numb with dismay.","Why ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌‌​​‌​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​‍did it still want to continue?","Couldn’t this System stop while it was ahead?","【What’s there to say?】 Jiang Yunxi put her hands on her hips like a tiny shrew. 【So what if my mother had someone she liked before she was married?","Who hasn’t had someone they admired when they were young?】","【I refuse to believe you’ve never had someone you liked, System.】","Madam Zheng felt warm inside.","People always said that daughters were their mothers’ little padded jackets, and it truly was the case.","Though it seemed her daughter had learned a rather eclectic assortment of things. How did she even know about youthful admiration?","It seemed that in the future...","The System said in a small voice, 【But the person your mother liked wasn’t your father!】","【So what if it wasn’t my father? My mother didn’t cheat on him or betray him.","Even if she had cheated on him, so what? Wouldn’t that mean my father had wronged her first?】","Madam Zheng’s face flushed.","Her daughter’s inner thoughts were far too bold. How could she say such things?","She didn’t know whether the Heir could hear her daughter’s thoughts either. If he could...","Madam Zheng didn’t dare imagine it.","As Madam Zheng trembled with anxiety, Jiang Yunxi continued to let her tongue run wild.","【My father is allowed to have wives and concubines, along with a whole bunch of legitimate and illegitimate children, but my mother isn’t allowed to have someone she likes?","If he hadn’t taken advantage of her when she was in a difficult position, my mother might be the principal wife of some other household by now.】","【My mother has done nothing wrong just because she had someone she liked. Even if she had eight or ten admirers, she still wouldn’t be in the wrong.","And that was before she married. Even if she had continued to—】","Seeing that her daughter was about to say something shocking, Madam Zheng hurriedly stopped her by deliberately calling out loudly toward the door,","“Has Physician Chen arrived yet?”","Her loud voice successfully interrupted Jiang Yunxi before she could finish.","A maid’s voice rang out from outside. “Madam, Physician Chen has arrived.”","Eager to dig up the physician’s gossip and recover her losses, Jiang Yunxi no longer had time to argue with the System.","【System, just remember one thing: my mother and I are on the same side. I’ll support her no matter what.】","Seriously, her father had four sons and three daughters. What rank did she even hold in his heart? She was probably at the very bottom.","But in her mother’s heart, she might not outrank her elder brother, but she was definitely second.","Jiang Yunxi had that much self-awareness.","【That’s enough gossip about my mother. Just give me the gossip points.】","The System felt aggrieved. There was still plenty it could say about Madam Zheng, but its host clearly didn’t want to listen anymore.","Fine. It would just have to find another opportunity later.","[Host, I’ll only say one thing.","No, make that two.]","Before the host could refuse, the System began speaking directly.","[Your maternal uncle is now an official at court. He serves as the Vice Commissioner of the Office of Transmission, a fourth-rank official with the authority to participate in state affairs and offer counsel.","Your younger maternal aunt entered the palace and is now Consort Duan. She has a son, a prince who is five by traditional Chinese reckoning—in other words, your cousin.]","[Holy crap.]","[Ding! The host has successfully uncovered gossip about her mother. Gossipy Points +200. Current Gossipy Points: 900.]"]},{"number":14,"title":"Chapter 14: The Imperial Prince Cousin Is a Death Warrant","paragraphs":["When Jiang Yunxi heard that her maternal uncle had also entered government service and now held a fourth-rank post, and that she even had a maternal aunt who had borne a prince, her mind went completely blank.","Just moments ago, she had been told that her maternal grandfather had been convicted of a crime, and that his entire family was relying on her father’s protection and financial support. She had even thought that her mother must be worried sick about her family and had been scrimping and saving every day to send money back home.","No wonder she wore hardly any jewelry. Her family must be short on money.","She had been thinking that if she married, she would have to find a way to bring along a generous dowry and spend the rest of her life doing nothing. Now it seemed even that hope was gone.","After all, she had read enough novels and watched enough television dramas to know that a concubine-born daughter’s dowry was usually paid only partly by the household treasury. The rest had to be saved up over the years, with additional help from her birth mother.","She was just thinking that she would have to find ways to make more money in the future when, in the very next moment, she became a relative of a prince—a member of the imperial clan.","The change was so sudden that she had no idea how to react.","With a prince for a younger cousin, could she perhaps just...","[Host, what are you daydreaming about? He’s only five by traditional reckoning. How is he supposed to protect you? The emperor has a whole harem and plenty of sons. Do you really think he’ll acknowledge you as an imperial relative?]","[Haven’t you seen those dramas? The unfavored consorts and princes live worse than servants. And you still want to...]","Madam Zheng frowned. What was a television drama?","And how could consorts and princes possibly live worse than servants?","Did this system, which had appeared out of nowhere, even know what it was talking about?","Madam Zheng wanted to angrily demand an explanation, but the moment she opened her mouth, she once again discovered that she could not make a sound.","Jiang Yunxi frowned. [My mother is so beautiful. My little aunt can’t possibly be anything less. How could she be unfavored?]","[If she were favored, would she only hold the position of a consort?]","[You know perfectly well that the inner palace and the imperial court are connected. Apart from your maternal uncle, does your little aunt have any other support in the court?]","[Perhaps she entered the palace for your maternal uncle’s sake!]","That was true. Just think of Consort Hua. If she had not had a powerful elder brother, she would never have been favored for so many years or acted so arrogantly in the imperial harem.","And ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​​‌​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​​‌​​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​​‌​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​​‌‌​‌​​‍Little Bird An had no powerful family behind her, so she could only be bullied by everyone.","[Think about why your maternal grandfather was convicted. Then think about your princely cousin. Do you still want to enjoy the benefits he brings?]","Jiang Yunxi’s good mood vanished completely.","[System, shouldn’t I be grateful that he’s still young and hasn’t been dragged into the struggle for the throne yet?]","[He’ll grow up eventually. Unless the throne changes hands before he comes of age, he won’t be able to escape it.","And because of your mother and you, the Marquis of Pingyang’s household—and even the family you marry into in the future—will be seen as being on his side. Even if you want to stay out of it, you won’t be able to.]","This time, even Madam Zheng could no longer remain calm.","As she watched Physician Chen enter with a young assistant and bow to her, she could only say woodenly, “Physician Chen, please examine Fifth Miss carefully.”","Thinking about the fate of the princes who had lost the struggle for the throne, as well as the fate of all those who had supported them, Jiang Yunxi instantly wilted like a balloon punctured by a needle.","Her future looked bleak. Jiang Yunxi wanted to run away again.","[System, do you think it’s too late for me to go back now?]","Returning to Huaxia would mean being reborn yet again, probably into another family that wasn’t particularly well-off, and inevitably becoming a corporate drone stuck working nine-to-nine, six days a week. But at least her life would be safe. She wouldn’t have to play a game where she could lose her head at any moment, or take part in some version of “let’s wipe out nine generations of the family.”","Madam Zheng frowned. Yunxi wanted to go back—but go back where? Wasn’t the marquis’s residence her home?","Seeing that things were going badly and fearing that her host might be frightened into running away again—or threaten to sever their bond and start squeezing every last benefit out of it—the system hurriedly tried to comfort her.","[Host, there’s no need to be afraid. You still have me.","As long as you gather gossip and save up plenty of gossip points, there are all kinds of life-saving items in the system store.]","[If you don’t want your cousin to get dragged into the struggle for the throne, find a way to meet him in the future and persuade him. If that doesn’t work, we can give him... you know.","Once the struggle for the throne is over, we’ll restore him.]","Jiang Yunxi raised an eyebrow. That did not sound like such a bad plan.","As long as she could keep herself alive, it would not hurt for her cousin to suffer a little.","Madam Zheng was frantic. You mangy system, what did you mean by “give him... you know”?","What were you planning to do to my nephew?","Just say it out loud! I swear I won’t beat you to death!","Yunxi, don’t let that wretched system fool you. He is your own flesh-and-blood cousin, and he is a prince. You must not listen to that system and hurt him.","If anyone finds out, the entire marquis’s household will...","The consequences would be no different from being dragged into the struggle for the throne.","Just then, a man entered the bedchamber, followed by a boy carrying a medicine chest. The system loudly reminded her,","[Host, the physician is here. Shall we dig up his gossip?]","For the sake of keeping her head attached to her neck, Jiang Yunxi clenched her teeth and decided that she had to gather as many gossip points as possible.","[Dig.]","She was having such a difficult time. Just moments ago, she had owed only 4,500 points. Now it looked as though the debt might multiply several times over.","Other people transmigrated into noble families with distinguished identities, legitimate births, and lives where they could simply lie back and enjoy themselves.","She had transmigrated as a concubine-born daughter, nearly died the moment she arrived, and found herself surrounded by wolves on every side.","She had a relative who seemed to possess an impressive status, but after taking a closer look—oh, he was actually a harbinger of death.","Madam Zheng hurriedly looked toward Physician Chen, wanting to confirm whether he could hear the system.","Judging from the reactions of the maids and older servants in the courtyard, they could not. But what if the physician could?","[Host, we’ve struck gold! There’s a huge secret.","Physician Chen has a huge secret.]","When she saw that neither Physician Chen nor his assistant showed the slightest change in expression, as if they had not heard a thing, Madam Zheng finally let out half the breath she had been holding.","The bed curtains had already been lowered. Jiang Yunxi’s hand extended beyond them, with a square of silk draped over her wrist.","She did not need to speak with Physician Chen herself, which suited the somewhat socially anxious Jiang Yunxi perfectly.","[What is it? System, hurry up and tell me.]","[Physician Chen’s name is Chen Zhiling. His family has practiced medicine for generations, and he began studying medicine from an early age.","But he has a rebellious streak. Ever since he was little, he never wanted to study medicine. He wanted to pursue literature and take the imperial examinations.","His family refused and insisted that he learn medicine. Neither side would give in, so in the end, they made him study both.]","Madam Zheng could not help sneaking a glance at Physician Chen, who was calmly examining her daughter’s pulse with his eyes closed.","She had not expected this seemingly mild-tempered man to be so stubborn. He had even refused to give in to his parents and elders.","He had supposedly wanted to pursue the civil examinations and enter government service, so how had he ended up becoming a physician after all?","Judging by his expression, he clearly had not heard her daughter’s thoughts. Otherwise, he would not be so calm.","Perhaps because mother and daughter were connected by heart, Jiang Yunxi asked the exact same question.","[Then how did he end up practicing medicine again? Did he eventually discover that he wasn’t cut out for studying?]","[Studying medicine is still studying, isn’t it? He was able to chew through such thick medical texts. The classics required for the civil examinations shouldn’t have been beyond him either.","Surely medical texts are much harder than those formulaic examination essays.]","[Host, don’t interrupt. You’ll understand once you let me finish.]","Jiang Yunxi was quite tolerant of the system when it was telling her gossip. Thus, she did not get angry. Instead, she said calmly,","[Go on, System. I promise I won’t interrupt.]","[Physician Chen is actually quite impressive. He studied two disciplines at once. At fifteen, he passed the prefectural-level examination and became a licentiate. At eighteen, he passed the provincial examination and became a provincial graduate.]","Jiang Yunxi worked it out based on the bits of ancient history she had picked up from TV dramas and novels.","[So does that mean he’ll have to take the metropolitan examination and then the palace examination before entering the court as an official?]","System: [That is correct.","But on his way to the capital to take the metropolitan examination, while passing through a stretch of mountain forest, an unexpected turn of events will occur.]","Now that’s more like it.","Jiang Yunxi clutched the quilt tighter.","Physician Chen frowned. “Fifth Miss, I’m only taking your pulse. Please relax.","Your heart is beating so fast that I can’t feel your pulse at all.”"]},{"number":15,"title":"Chapter 15: Dr. Chen of the Chen Manor, the Bandit Chief's Son-in-Law","paragraphs":["Madam Zheng listened to the System’s gossip and found herself on edge as well.","When she heard what Physician Chen had to say, she realized that her daughter might have fallen into the same trap as she had. She hurriedly said, “Yunxi, don’t let your imagination run wild. The physician just said your fever has gone down considerably. It won’t burn your brain. Just relax and let Physician Chen examine your pulse properly.”","What Madam Zheng was really thinking was: Yunxi, don’t let the System continue gossiping for now. Wait until after your pulse has been examined.","A pulse examination took a full quarter of an hour. If anything went wrong halfway through, they would have to start all over again.","Going back and forth like that would waste far too much time.","The mother and daughter were on exactly the same wavelength. Jiang Yunxi hurriedly reminded the System,","[System, wait a little longer before you continue. Let me finish having my pulse examined first.]","Although she was dying to know what happened next, Jiang Yunxi still forcibly suppressed her gossip-loving soul and made herself relax so Physician Chen could examine her pulse.","After finally completing the examination, the maid tucked her hand back beneath the quilt. Jiang Yunxi had no interest in listening to the results and hurriedly asked,","[System, hurry up and tell me! What unforeseen event happened to Physician Chen on his way to the capital for the imperial examinations?]","As for the results of the examination, with all those medicines produced by the System, she wouldn’t have any problems anyway. Who had the patience to listen to Physician Chen ramble on with a bunch of medical theories she couldn’t understand?","Madam Zheng also wanted to hear the System continue, but she still had to listen to her daughter’s medical report.","Unlike Jiang Yunxi, she did not have complete faith in the System’s medicines.","[Physician Chen encountered bandits who were robbing travelers.]","Jiang Yunxi had watched analyses on short-video platforms before. According to those analyses, bandits in ancient times generally wouldn’t rob candidates traveling to the capital for the imperial examinations.","First, candidates traveling to the capital for the examinations carried a yellow banner bearing the words “Imperial Examination by Order of His Majesty” or “Ministry of Rites Examination.” It symbolized that they were traveling under the emperor’s orders. Robbing them was tantamount to defying imperial authority.","Second, candidates who had passed the provincial examination already qualified as reserve officials and might become government officials in the future.","The bandits feared that if they robbed such a person, they would suffer retaliation later—or even provoke the imperial court into launching an extermination campaign against them.","Jiang Yunxi asked: [Even if Physician Chen encountered bandits robbing travelers, once they learned he was a candidate on his way to the capital for the examinations, they wouldn’t do anything to him, would they?]","[Under ordinary circumstances, that would indeed be the case.","But unfortunately, Physician Chen happened to encounter a special circumstance.]","[What special circumstance?] Jiang Yunxi immediately grew interested.","[If not for the fact that this particular bandit group had a female chief who took a liking to Physician Chen because he was young and handsome, then...]","Madam Zheng coughed several times.","Physician Chen asked, “Madam, what’s wrong?”","Madam Zheng waved her hand. “Nothing, nothing. I accidentally choked on my saliva.”","Jiang Yunxi thought: [My mother is still like a child. She can even choke on her saliva while talking.","I never do that.]","Madam Zheng clenched her fist. “It’s all because of you, you little ingrate.","I ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​​‌​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​​‌​​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​​‌​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​​‌‌​‌​​‍wonder if you’ve been reading too many romance stories lately. You’ve actually picked up all sorts of indecent ideas.”","“Looks like I’ll have to be more careful from now on. Yunxi isn’t allowed to read those trashy stories anymore. They’ve completely warped her temperament.”","Seeing that Madam Zheng was all right, Jiang Yunxi urged the System on,","[System, hurry up and tell me! Did some female bandit chief take a fancy to Physician Chen and want to drag him up the mountain to become her husband?]","The System replied: [There was no female bandit chief or bandit chieftain’s husband, but there was a bandit chieftain’s son-in-law.]","[The bandit chief had no sons, only one daughter. She loved reading stories about talented scholars and beautiful maidens and wanted to marry a scholar.","But she was the bandit chief’s daughter. Which scholar would be willing to marry her?","Then they just happened to run into Physician Chen, that unlucky fellow. He was not only a scholar, but a provincial graduate on his way to the capital for the examinations—far more impressive than an ordinary scholar.","Those bandits wanted to curry favor with their young mistress, so they tied him up, hauled him up the mountain, and presented him to her.]","Jiang Yunxi’s mind had already conjured up a scene of a beautiful woman forcing herself on a scholar—a scene that would need to be censored before anyone could watch it.","[What happened afterward? Did Physician Chen submit?] she asked impatiently.","Madam Zheng stole a glance at Physician Chen.","“Physician Chen has been living in our residence for all these years, but I’ve never heard of him having a wife. He does have a son, though.”","[Let me tell you, Host. The story between those two was absolutely spectacular. First they... then they... and finally they...]","Jiang Yunxi’s strange laughter grew louder and louder as she exclaimed,","[System, be more detailed. Explain it properly.]","[System, how did the bandit chieftain’s daughter overpower him? What position did they use? Be specific.]","[System, you can’t just skim over this part. Go on, tell me...]","Madam Zheng’s face grew darker and darker. Several times, she opened her mouth to speak, but no words came out.","Her expression left Physician Chen and all the maids and matrons nearby utterly baffled.","Fifth Miss was already in much better condition than she had been yesterday. Yet judging from Madam Zheng’s expression, she seemed even less satisfied.","In fact, she looked even more dissatisfied than yesterday.","What exactly did Madam Zheng think? Did she feel that Fifth Miss shouldn’t have recovered, or that she was recovering too slowly?","But comparing her attitude yesterday with today, it really did look as though she felt Fifth Miss shouldn’t have gotten better at all.","Could it be that Madam Zheng thought Fifth Miss’s frail body, constantly falling ill every few days and dragging her down, would be better off if she simply didn’t survive this time?","Fifth Miss had been harmed by someone from the Marchioness’s household. If Fifth Miss truly failed to recover, Madam Zheng and her son could use the Marchioness’s guilt to obtain quite a few benefits.","Oh, heavens! Madam Zheng usually appeared to be such a loving mother, always showing Fifth Miss how much she cared about her. Who would have thought she was actually this kind of person?","Madam Zheng had no idea that her dark expression, caused by hearing her daughter’s rather bold and rather scandalous words, had ruined her reputation.","Everyone else had already assumed she was planning to use her daughter’s death to gain power and benefits.","[That’s how the two of them really got together, and the bandit chieftain’s daughter became pregnant.]","[Unfortunately, the bandit chieftain’s daughter later died in childbirth. There was no doctor on the mountain, and Physician Chen was the only one there. Although he did his best, he still couldn’t save her.","Fortunately, he was able to save their son.]","Hearing this, even Jiang Yunxi couldn’t help sighing.","The two of them had clearly come to love each other. They had wanted to spend the rest of their lives together. Why couldn’t Heaven have let them?","[Later, another bandit group took a fancy to that mountain stronghold because of its dangerous terrain. The original bandits were no match for them. Most of them were killed, while the rest fled down the mountain to save their lives.","To protect his son-in-law and grandson, the bandit chief suffered severe injuries. Physician Chen did everything he could to treat him, but he still failed to save him.]","[Why didn’t he take the imperial examinations again after coming down the mountain?]","The System replied: [He had spent several years living in a bandit’s den. How could he explain that to anyone?","If he told the truth, his son would become the son of a bandit. And afterward...]","[In fact, that entire bandit group had originally gone up into the mountains because they had been driven to it by famine. They had only done so to survive and hadn’t committed any truly heinous acts.","They were all dead. Why make it so that their names would never rest in peace even after death?]","[His wife had risked her life to give birth to their son.","His father-in-law had treated him well throughout all those years and had ultimately sacrificed his own life to protect him and his son. How could Physician Chen bear to ruin their reputations after death?]","[Physician Chen regretted only that his medical skills had been inadequate and that he had been unable to save his wife and father-in-law.","After that, he gave up on the imperial examinations and devoted himself to studying medicine.","He feared that if he took another wife, his second wife might mistreat the son whom his wife and father-in-law had given their lives to protect. So he never remarried and raised his son alone.]","Through the bed curtains and folding screen, Jiang Yunxi watched Physician Chen’s silhouette as he wrote out the prescription.","【System, Physician Chen really is a good man. The Eldest Miss didn’t choose the wrong man to abduct as her husband!】","System: 【He certainly is a good man—and a good father.】","Madam Zheng couldn’t help agreeing inwardly.","Jiang Yunxi: 【He’s much better than my deadbeat father.】","System: Are you really brave enough to let your father hear that?"]}]);
